[[:db/retract 17592186148895 :answer-field/choices 17592186148896] [:db/retract 17592186148895 :answer-field/choices 17592186148897] [:db/retract 17592186148895 :answer-field/choices 17592186148898] [:db/retract 17592186148895 :answer-field/choices 17592186148899] [:db/retract 17592186148895 :answer-field/choices 17592186148900] {:db/id 17592186152152 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b7b6e192-3a06-52fc-8d5f-7a6810288b2c" "question-1acef96d-8256-5e1a-85ce-bb35520d6331" "question-6b6196d0-946b-5675-b1cf-30fba169b2db"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152151 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-003282d8-d3cb-54da-a9af-399e3a75da3b" "question-e0e69171-a8d5-534f-acb8-6c56c972aa07" "question-50cce965-116a-5091-8060-d4b135e273bd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152150 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f88ad5cd-8533-5739-b1c9-9a040c2e3b2c" "question-e4fe7c63-ddd1-59b8-9a3b-8f1a0e46d1f0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152394 :question/problem "![](images/ac/ac4970f243e32138114e2f8973205d39e75ed95445a0b410e969e494672d2b37.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $3$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{13}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{13}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{13})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =2\\cdot {M}_{11}+2\\cdot {M}_{12}+2\\cdot {M}_{13} \\\\  & =2({M}_{11}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{13}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186148895 :answer-field/correct "answer-5a7eda2c-a027-5f95-97f6-e15eace33722" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5a7eda2c-a027-5f95-97f6-e15eace33722" "answer-d79c99a8-657e-5f1b-9bf1-7b78ca1c5271" "answer-e0699502-562e-5567-92d0-a0fdd69f0682" "answer-d9dffb21-59c0-5a1f-8919-0d8e4cb108a1" "answer-548eea5d-4b28-5e16-b164-434012c34f08"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a7eda2c-a027-5f95-97f6-e15eace33722" :answer/id #uuid "5a7eda2c-a027-5f95-97f6-e15eace33722" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({M}_{11}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{13})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d79c99a8-657e-5f1b-9bf1-7b78ca1c5271" :answer/id #uuid "d79c99a8-657e-5f1b-9bf1-7b78ca1c5271" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{M}_{11}+2{M}_{12}+{M}_{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0699502-562e-5567-92d0-a0fdd69f0682" :answer/id #uuid "e0699502-562e-5567-92d0-a0fdd69f0682" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{M}_{11}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9dffb21-59c0-5a1f-8919-0d8e4cb108a1" :answer/id #uuid "d9dffb21-59c0-5a1f-8919-0d8e4cb108a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{M}_{11}-{M}_{12}-{M}_{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-548eea5d-4b28-5e16-b164-434012c34f08" :answer/id #uuid "548eea5d-4b28-5e16-b164-434012c34f08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{M}_{11}\\cdot {M}_{12}\\cdot {M}_{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b7b6e192-3a06-52fc-8d5f-7a6810288b2c" :question/id #uuid "b7b6e192-3a06-52fc-8d5f-7a6810288b2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-123058" :question/problem "![](images/dd/dd73cb7785de514503cba6a04931a88084172b58826efdf22ea847f256c375fb.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $2$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =4\\cdot {M}_{11}+4\\cdot {M}_{12} \\\\  & =4({M}_{11}+{M}_{12}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fea3a60f-daf8-541c-b5ca-7c7fb29e64dc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fea3a60f-daf8-541c-b5ca-7c7fb29e64dc" :answer-field/id #uuid "fea3a60f-daf8-541c-b5ca-7c7fb29e64dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-013eb8ba-2e75-572b-b420-54178b0eb197" :answer-field/choices ["answer-013eb8ba-2e75-572b-b420-54178b0eb197" "answer-ea08442c-fd3b-5555-a6e4-c06d13e975c4" "answer-c5b9a51f-45a8-5f29-bd32-e075b761e09e" "answer-cde0b272-300e-514e-be66-91ac196872ef" "answer-7f3d9435-4690-5e73-b1cf-047a2751112a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-013eb8ba-2e75-572b-b420-54178b0eb197" :answer/id #uuid "013eb8ba-2e75-572b-b420-54178b0eb197" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4({M}_{11}+{M}_{12})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea08442c-fd3b-5555-a6e4-c06d13e975c4" :answer/id #uuid "ea08442c-fd3b-5555-a6e4-c06d13e975c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{M}_{11}+{M}_{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5b9a51f-45a8-5f29-bd32-e075b761e09e" :answer/id #uuid "c5b9a51f-45a8-5f29-bd32-e075b761e09e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{M}_{11}+4{M}_{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cde0b272-300e-514e-be66-91ac196872ef" :answer/id #uuid "cde0b272-300e-514e-be66-91ac196872ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{M}_{11}+{M}_{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f3d9435-4690-5e73-b1cf-047a2751112a" :answer/id #uuid "7f3d9435-4690-5e73-b1cf-047a2751112a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{M}_{12}-{M}_{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1acef96d-8256-5e1a-85ce-bb35520d6331" :question/id #uuid "1acef96d-8256-5e1a-85ce-bb35520d6331" :question/math-academy-id "q-123125" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a4ab905de5bed2182757fa11a1945bbffec175b314918b3581d2ae062d64cdcc.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $3$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{31})=15.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =15\\cdot {M}_{11}+15\\cdot {M}_{21}+15\\cdot {M}_{31} \\\\  & =15({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6aa326de-d714-5b39-9140-e8acb0109c83"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6aa326de-d714-5b39-9140-e8acb0109c83" :answer-field/id #uuid "6aa326de-d714-5b39-9140-e8acb0109c83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-01d4ba0e-ab3b-5599-869a-41c3240198d5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-01d4ba0e-ab3b-5599-869a-41c3240198d5" "answer-c67b7698-5934-5992-8207-9d8f7538d1b5" "answer-4d2e9ef1-c4da-5fc7-be4b-026f8b0e945d" "answer-5fd2e9bb-e861-580e-9f16-5b718d107429" "answer-90b1f25d-f8da-5944-b0cb-c5c49e1e39ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01d4ba0e-ab3b-5599-869a-41c3240198d5" :answer/id #uuid "01d4ba0e-ab3b-5599-869a-41c3240198d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c67b7698-5934-5992-8207-9d8f7538d1b5" :answer/id #uuid "c67b7698-5934-5992-8207-9d8f7538d1b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15{M}_{11}+5{M}_{21}+3{M}_{31}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d2e9ef1-c4da-5fc7-be4b-026f8b0e945d" :answer/id #uuid "4d2e9ef1-c4da-5fc7-be4b-026f8b0e945d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fd2e9bb-e861-580e-9f16-5b718d107429" :answer/id #uuid "5fd2e9bb-e861-580e-9f16-5b718d107429" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90b1f25d-f8da-5944-b0cb-c5c49e1e39ed" :answer/id #uuid "90b1f25d-f8da-5944-b0cb-c5c49e1e39ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{M}_{11}+3{M}_{21}-{M}_{31}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6b6196d0-946b-5675-b1cf-30fba169b2db" :question/id #uuid "6b6196d0-946b-5675-b1cf-30fba169b2db" :question/math-academy-id "q-123056" :question/problem "![](images/6d/6dcc08ca41977f189d4e873be6c060b3d8f446fb3ba2e4b0ee2667403ebb07fc.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31})+{M}_{41}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{41}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{31})=\\text{Area}({R}_{41})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =2\\cdot {M}_{11}+2\\cdot {M}_{21}+2\\cdot {M}_{31}+2\\cdot {M}_{41} \\\\  & =2({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}+{M}_{41}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-57f9cf12-8dfb-53b1-b292-86ced016edb6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-57f9cf12-8dfb-53b1-b292-86ced016edb6" :answer-field/id #uuid "57f9cf12-8dfb-53b1-b292-86ced016edb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-23926a61-03a3-5461-9946-25ae62757cb3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-23926a61-03a3-5461-9946-25ae62757cb3" "answer-dca45719-25c3-5ae1-83e9-c4706be64e6a" "answer-88571423-517e-51ee-b66f-67c0f785fd03" "answer-80a9b97e-e4af-5c15-9693-da5015493b5c" "answer-97812a4d-76b5-5d6e-b1ae-dc5df4c4141b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23926a61-03a3-5461-9946-25ae62757cb3" :answer/id #uuid "23926a61-03a3-5461-9946-25ae62757cb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}+{M}_{41})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dca45719-25c3-5ae1-83e9-c4706be64e6a" :answer/id #uuid "dca45719-25c3-5ae1-83e9-c4706be64e6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}+2{M}_{41}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88571423-517e-51ee-b66f-67c0f785fd03" :answer/id #uuid "88571423-517e-51ee-b66f-67c0f785fd03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{M}_{11}+2{M}_{21}+2{M}_{31}+{M}_{41}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80a9b97e-e4af-5c15-9693-da5015493b5c" :answer/id #uuid "80a9b97e-e4af-5c15-9693-da5015493b5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}+{M}_{41}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97812a4d-76b5-5d6e-b1ae-dc5df4c4141b" :answer/id #uuid "97812a4d-76b5-5d6e-b1ae-dc5df4c4141b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{M}_{11}\\cdot {M}_{21}\\cdot {M}_{31}\\cdot {M}_{41}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-003282d8-d3cb-54da-a9af-399e3a75da3b" :question/id #uuid "003282d8-d3cb-54da-a9af-399e3a75da3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-75234" :question/problem "Let $R=[-3,-1]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=10-4x-2y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{-3,-2,-1\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/10/10eca85fc2ab60ea0b1ee229b0a0e20110f88c4724088c0f0630d22150a8a08d.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}+{M}_{41}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=10-4x-2y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=10-4x-2y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ea/eaa3ed265eac5a53eedc07f07e2ff386505a6ea5cc4934653d587e84238b540d.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/c3/c332690fba1843ee09bd1466f1c978c41aff8438bf9b2a23a847ca58e2f9c228.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(-3,1)=20 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(-2,1)=16 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(-3,2)=18 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(-2,2)=14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =20+16+18+14 \\\\  & =68.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1d634307-c7b5-59ff-9b60-846917abd3ed"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1d634307-c7b5-59ff-9b60-846917abd3ed" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d634307-c7b5-59ff-9b60-846917abd3ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-50aeb266-ab0d-5212-9160-89d504220b88" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8d1a5a83-6b20-57f5-b4fb-8472a5b67928" "answer-7b106611-ae0e-5111-91d1-a39c2610f56d" "answer-342a7334-6ebf-59b7-8331-37af5e6b4d2c" "answer-de92d4f3-fc6c-5524-b29c-1a39a0e93889" "answer-50aeb266-ab0d-5212-9160-89d504220b88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d1a5a83-6b20-57f5-b4fb-8472a5b67928" :answer/id #uuid "8d1a5a83-6b20-57f5-b4fb-8472a5b67928" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b106611-ae0e-5111-91d1-a39c2610f56d" :answer/id #uuid "7b106611-ae0e-5111-91d1-a39c2610f56d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-342a7334-6ebf-59b7-8331-37af5e6b4d2c" :answer/id #uuid "342a7334-6ebf-59b7-8331-37af5e6b4d2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de92d4f3-fc6c-5524-b29c-1a39a0e93889" :answer/id #uuid "de92d4f3-fc6c-5524-b29c-1a39a0e93889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-50aeb266-ab0d-5212-9160-89d504220b88" :answer/id #uuid "50aeb266-ab0d-5212-9160-89d504220b88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "68" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e0e69171-a8d5-534f-acb8-6c56c972aa07" :question/id #uuid "e0e69171-a8d5-534f-acb8-6c56c972aa07" :question/math-academy-id "q-123243" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,5]\\times [1,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=100-{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,5\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,3,5\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/77/77fdf238fb2b4046da6ddc69024378a56e4de5f46de301d5fac094cbc290b23b.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=10$ for both subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =10\\cdot {M}_{11}+10\\cdot {M}_{12} \\\\  & =10({M}_{11}+{M}_{12}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=100-{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=100-{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/62/62871cd2fcc4993e0775fb7bdf0609d7849a1aa2ea5a314bc727967df590d6e7.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/9b/9b814374a5b132560656d6fe2dc2350cb693847733a40c0d21b9a13be30025e1.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(0,1)=97 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(0,3)=73\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =10(97+73) \\\\  & =1\\,700.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0cc8f80d-aaaf-5d96-872e-79594ef03ec3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0cc8f80d-aaaf-5d96-872e-79594ef03ec3" :answer-field/id #uuid "0cc8f80d-aaaf-5d96-872e-79594ef03ec3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1554cd6c-bc48-5357-bfb6-fd992f56f2c9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9a87d8cc-135e-5a20-8918-9957d54d7ef4" "answer-c2224caf-3cbf-5e50-a2f8-443aa9d623a4" "answer-15957473-8159-5ecd-bb20-e1513dd4ecde" "answer-d3edb6e3-1c8e-5e1f-8baa-842b14f66295" "answer-1554cd6c-bc48-5357-bfb6-fd992f56f2c9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a87d8cc-135e-5a20-8918-9957d54d7ef4" :answer/id #uuid "9a87d8cc-135e-5a20-8918-9957d54d7ef4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "135" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2224caf-3cbf-5e50-a2f8-443aa9d623a4" :answer/id #uuid "c2224caf-3cbf-5e50-a2f8-443aa9d623a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "170" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15957473-8159-5ecd-bb20-e1513dd4ecde" :answer/id #uuid "15957473-8159-5ecd-bb20-e1513dd4ecde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,350" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3edb6e3-1c8e-5e1f-8baa-842b14f66295" :answer/id #uuid "d3edb6e3-1c8e-5e1f-8baa-842b14f66295" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,400" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1554cd6c-bc48-5357-bfb6-fd992f56f2c9" :answer/id #uuid "1554cd6c-bc48-5357-bfb6-fd992f56f2c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,700" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-50cce965-116a-5091-8060-d4b135e273bd" :question/id #uuid "50cce965-116a-5091-8060-d4b135e273bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-123232" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,5]\\times [0,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=10-x-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3,4,5\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,1\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/5b/5bd8200cb0f0aa8ca38548ae731acb54d7118e3ca735ebd5e4aebe5b6a7aa1b5.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31})+{M}_{41}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{41}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}+{M}_{41}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=10-x-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=10-x-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/cc/cc616280fc457f14441e30a9e551eacf73bd56de02e68ced200302cbb1db68ac.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/e2/e2e1ab24e5d73cfc6414d7e01cd2d2d923f0f73bca137e65c9968b9142360389.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(1,0)=9 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(2,0)=8 \\\\ {M}_{31} & =f(3,0)=7 \\\\ {M}_{41} & =f(4,0)=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =9+8+7+6 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2fc70692-4870-59d7-8ebd-70a7bca018cb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2fc70692-4870-59d7-8ebd-70a7bca018cb" :answer-field/id #uuid "2fc70692-4870-59d7-8ebd-70a7bca018cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b22e9aaf-cb1e-5405-8f98-df2a5454337d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7c4eb9aa-414e-5ce6-bdbf-2a9bea7a24d7" "answer-b22e9aaf-cb1e-5405-8f98-df2a5454337d" "answer-39917bfb-b047-56d8-b47c-c5ec66b1e25b" "answer-443a2ad6-b0fb-5a5a-a98a-17ea5dd555e1" "answer-f946a5c4-dc1b-5486-a418-99decd3f1256"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c4eb9aa-414e-5ce6-bdbf-2a9bea7a24d7" :answer/id #uuid "7c4eb9aa-414e-5ce6-bdbf-2a9bea7a24d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b22e9aaf-cb1e-5405-8f98-df2a5454337d" :answer/id #uuid "b22e9aaf-cb1e-5405-8f98-df2a5454337d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39917bfb-b047-56d8-b47c-c5ec66b1e25b" :answer/id #uuid "39917bfb-b047-56d8-b47c-c5ec66b1e25b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-443a2ad6-b0fb-5a5a-a98a-17ea5dd555e1" :answer/id #uuid "443a2ad6-b0fb-5a5a-a98a-17ea5dd555e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f946a5c4-dc1b-5486-a418-99decd3f1256" :answer/id #uuid "f946a5c4-dc1b-5486-a418-99decd3f1256" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f88ad5cd-8533-5739-b1c9-9a040c2e3b2c" :question/id #uuid "f88ad5cd-8533-5739-b1c9-9a040c2e3b2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-75045" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+y+2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{-1,0,1\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{-1,0,1\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/0c/0c68391a7a23867f21ee851aa86d389ff4dc186c3aaedde0ccb1fe15b5b4ee5b.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y+2$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y+2$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/14/144142b823e7db82eb9b65e6ddc835d75a7fd8d218eab17f9db9019c4b8ab109.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/a2/a2c948117d63fdd60d16ac29b3900238f7c246201bd45df3e3ee940aac0d4ee6.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(0,0)=2 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(1,0)=3 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(0,1)=3 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(1,1)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =2+3+3+4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f8792aef-971c-524f-813b-450f77f5e710"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f8792aef-971c-524f-813b-450f77f5e710" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8792aef-971c-524f-813b-450f77f5e710" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b4e04a2c-361f-56eb-bed1-233836e23e41" :answer-field/choices ["answer-47143193-8197-59a4-a2da-4be68703689e" "answer-b4e04a2c-361f-56eb-bed1-233836e23e41" "answer-c4e8b813-b4ae-570d-81ba-bcfa60a66d90" "answer-b5ec27bf-c690-5989-8d49-e61940286e53" "answer-4ff307b3-0cf9-5782-bf27-1ba7036e9b66"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47143193-8197-59a4-a2da-4be68703689e" :answer/id #uuid "47143193-8197-59a4-a2da-4be68703689e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4e04a2c-361f-56eb-bed1-233836e23e41" :answer/id #uuid "b4e04a2c-361f-56eb-bed1-233836e23e41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4e8b813-b4ae-570d-81ba-bcfa60a66d90" :answer/id #uuid "c4e8b813-b4ae-570d-81ba-bcfa60a66d90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5ec27bf-c690-5989-8d49-e61940286e53" :answer/id #uuid "b5ec27bf-c690-5989-8d49-e61940286e53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ff307b3-0cf9-5782-bf27-1ba7036e9b66" :answer/id #uuid "4ff307b3-0cf9-5782-bf27-1ba7036e9b66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e4fe7c63-ddd1-59b8-9a3b-8f1a0e46d1f0" :question/id #uuid "e4fe7c63-ddd1-59b8-9a3b-8f1a0e46d1f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-75184" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+5.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/6f/6fc1abc4b93b59eda024e126f8503b23f067bd9ea086a0256fcd3e67dfd7200a.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+5$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+5$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/7d/7dbec95d53ae55a09ab0a941c69f506f11be6e645a03aca3095bede1b3e966f8.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/5e/5edcabe01ac87d115a69a8b842c537187b1f1d2a003664e5fb68f7e70db3ae3d.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(2,2)=17 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(3,2)=27 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(2,3)=22 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(3,3)=32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =17+27+22+32 \\\\  & =98.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4fb061b0-ea4e-5a2f-871b-5b70b09fe31c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4fb061b0-ea4e-5a2f-871b-5b70b09fe31c" :answer-field/id #uuid "4fb061b0-ea4e-5a2f-871b-5b70b09fe31c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f04285fe-0309-56d8-804f-d0e703b8541f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-84adaa8f-d6bb-51e6-a982-60965661513b" "answer-f2f66292-0731-5d0f-b07b-26cc33e74a7f" "answer-8761081f-ad94-57ba-80a7-1efbf007857c" "answer-7ce39bb5-a799-5b6e-9a15-dceec85eb578" "answer-f04285fe-0309-56d8-804f-d0e703b8541f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84adaa8f-d6bb-51e6-a982-60965661513b" :answer/id #uuid "84adaa8f-d6bb-51e6-a982-60965661513b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "39" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2f66292-0731-5d0f-b07b-26cc33e74a7f" :answer/id #uuid "f2f66292-0731-5d0f-b07b-26cc33e74a7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "49" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8761081f-ad94-57ba-80a7-1efbf007857c" :answer/id #uuid "8761081f-ad94-57ba-80a7-1efbf007857c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ce39bb5-a799-5b6e-9a15-dceec85eb578" :answer/id #uuid "7ce39bb5-a799-5b6e-9a15-dceec85eb578" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "88" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f04285fe-0309-56d8-804f-d0e703b8541f" :answer/id #uuid "f04285fe-0309-56d8-804f-d0e703b8541f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "98" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192844 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6cb83115-237f-5265-8ee0-e3661c1aa677"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6cb83115-237f-5265-8ee0-e3661c1aa677" :question/id #uuid "6cb83115-237f-5265-8ee0-e3661c1aa677" :question/math-academy-id "q-154330" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $8>-3y-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $1$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & >-3y-1 \\\\ 8+1 & >-3y-1+1 \\\\ 9 & >-3y+0 \\\\ 9 & >-3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-3.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9\\,\\, & >\\,\\,-3y \\\\ \\frac{9}{-3}\\, & <\\,\\,\\frac{-3y}{-3} \\\\ -3\\, & <\\,\\,\\frac{\\cancel{-3}y}{\\cancel{-3}} \\\\ -3\\, & <\\,\\,y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember, we also need to flip the inequality.\n\n$$\ny>-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y>-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-309cb488-1b6e-5abd-9b12-84b31690a593"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-309cb488-1b6e-5abd-9b12-84b31690a593" :answer-field/id #uuid "309cb488-1b6e-5abd-9b12-84b31690a593" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-57a09a4a-eca2-51d2-adf2-83b39061ac56" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2824e734-1d0e-59ba-9fa3-74ca7138f894" "answer-8ff2dbd3-daef-550b-944a-1e868b75ca46" "answer-2194c414-3f47-5f2b-ac54-1499746d5c9d" "answer-57a09a4a-eca2-51d2-adf2-83b39061ac56" "answer-687c3b63-c49a-5b4f-a05a-69ec916c4557"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2824e734-1d0e-59ba-9fa3-74ca7138f894" :answer/id #uuid "2824e734-1d0e-59ba-9fa3-74ca7138f894" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y<-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ff2dbd3-daef-550b-944a-1e868b75ca46" :answer/id #uuid "8ff2dbd3-daef-550b-944a-1e868b75ca46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y<3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2194c414-3f47-5f2b-ac54-1499746d5c9d" :answer/id #uuid "2194c414-3f47-5f2b-ac54-1499746d5c9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y<\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57a09a4a-eca2-51d2-adf2-83b39061ac56" :answer/id #uuid "57a09a4a-eca2-51d2-adf2-83b39061ac56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y>-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-687c3b63-c49a-5b4f-a05a-69ec916c4557" :answer/id #uuid "687c3b63-c49a-5b4f-a05a-69ec916c4557" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y>-\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192843 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6bc91ea0-3fcd-5fed-9f63-f013dbd34da2" "question-b84140b5-0b6b-54d3-81ed-16117dd9ce00"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6bc91ea0-3fcd-5fed-9f63-f013dbd34da2" :question/id #uuid "6bc91ea0-3fcd-5fed-9f63-f013dbd34da2" :question/math-academy-id "q-176017" :question/problem "The solution to the inequality $-4x+5<-7$ is $x${{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $5$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x+5 & <-7 \\\\ -4x+5-5 & <-7-5 \\\\ -4x+0 & <-12 \\\\ -4x & <-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-4.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x\\,\\, & <\\,\\,-12 \\\\ \\frac{-4x}{-4}\\, & >\\,\\,\\frac{-12}{-4} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-4}x}{\\cancel{-4}}\\, & >\\,\\,3 \\\\ x\\,\\, & >\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x>3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-28989681-8083-513e-8cb9-ac9e3a421813" "answer-field-634bfe49-e89b-5d75-a701-ef10907af9e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28989681-8083-513e-8cb9-ac9e3a421813" :answer-field/id #uuid "28989681-8083-513e-8cb9-ac9e3a421813" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6b6d4d1f-fe13-5d6f-ad23-9e6fdadd762f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6b6d4d1f-fe13-5d6f-ad23-9e6fdadd762f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b6d4d1f-fe13-5d6f-ad23-9e6fdadd762f" :answer/id #uuid "6b6d4d1f-fe13-5d6f-ad23-9e6fdadd762f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value ">" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-634bfe49-e89b-5d75-a701-ef10907af9e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "634bfe49-e89b-5d75-a701-ef10907af9e4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0128a262-82a1-5207-9efa-8d990c844899" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0128a262-82a1-5207-9efa-8d990c844899"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0128a262-82a1-5207-9efa-8d990c844899" :answer/id #uuid "0128a262-82a1-5207-9efa-8d990c844899" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b84140b5-0b6b-54d3-81ed-16117dd9ce00" :question/id #uuid "b84140b5-0b6b-54d3-81ed-16117dd9ce00" :question/math-academy-id "q-176019" :question/problem "The solution to the inequality $-2x+10\\ge 4$ is $x${{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $10$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+10 & \\ge 4 \\\\ -2x+10-10 & \\ge 4-10 \\\\ -2x+0 & \\ge -6 \\\\ -2x & \\ge -6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-2.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,-6 \\\\ \\frac{-2x}{-2}\\, & \\le \\,\\,\\frac{-6}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-2}x}{\\cancel{-2}}\\, & \\le \\,\\,3 \\\\ x\\,\\, & \\le \\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\le 3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-04e9947e-f17a-5a85-9520-49f3ca6f1715" "answer-field-7bf29e7a-3d2a-5b89-a970-2efcbd44a944"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-04e9947e-f17a-5a85-9520-49f3ca6f1715" :answer-field/id #uuid "04e9947e-f17a-5a85-9520-49f3ca6f1715" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b3b21fd7-3a01-5064-9900-f721f255ee82" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b3b21fd7-3a01-5064-9900-f721f255ee82"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3b21fd7-3a01-5064-9900-f721f255ee82" :answer/id #uuid "b3b21fd7-3a01-5064-9900-f721f255ee82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7bf29e7a-3d2a-5b89-a970-2efcbd44a944" :answer-field/id #uuid "7bf29e7a-3d2a-5b89-a970-2efcbd44a944" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1e1ec133-84cc-5dfd-ab86-4c990c6b8e05" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1e1ec133-84cc-5dfd-ab86-4c990c6b8e05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e1ec133-84cc-5dfd-ab86-4c990c6b8e05" :answer/id #uuid "1e1ec133-84cc-5dfd-ab86-4c990c6b8e05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a0d62477-1126-5c13-a77b-0fb8dc71b298" :activity/id #uuid "a0d62477-1126-5c13-a77b-0fb8dc71b298" :activity/title "Solving Two-Step Inequalities" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050503 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-0b6c0382-e0e6-5a11-acdd-801c9c98f6d5" "step-206bf70a-edd4-5336-bda0-885ad4c20a15" "step-974300c1-4dd6-59e1-b165-c4b71f32045c"] :activity/first-step "step-0b6c0382-e0e6-5a11-acdd-801c9c98f6d5" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-0b6c0382-e0e6-5a11-acdd-801c9c98f6d5" :step/id #uuid "0b6c0382-e0e6-5a11-acdd-801c9c98f6d5" :step/content "question-6cb83115-237f-5265-8ee0-e3661c1aa677" :step/next "step-206bf70a-edd4-5336-bda0-885ad4c20a15" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-206bf70a-edd4-5336-bda0-885ad4c20a15" :step/id #uuid "206bf70a-edd4-5336-bd