:db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4a70c3e-7778-5f34-82d7-f5260b8d83b1" :answer/id #uuid "b4a70c3e-7778-5f34-82d7-f5260b8d83b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,0,0)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186378921 :answer-field/choices ["answer-19d58279-abc1-50a8-9085-0ebd005374af" "answer-51a5d90e-ca90-5c73-accf-e4213a388f0c" "answer-dc655d9f-5706-5e04-a2b6-a021fd9f2af0" "answer-06f58c8d-dd36-54da-a7cb-4e0680dd8d11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19d58279-abc1-50a8-9085-0ebd005374af" :answer/id #uuid "19d58279-abc1-50a8-9085-0ebd005374af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}<1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51a5d90e-ca90-5c73-accf-e4213a388f0c" :answer/id #uuid "51a5d90e-ca90-5c73-accf-e4213a388f0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}>1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc655d9f-5706-5e04-a2b6-a021fd9f2af0" :answer/id #uuid "dc655d9f-5706-5e04-a2b6-a021fd9f2af0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06f58c8d-dd36-54da-a7cb-4e0680dd8d11" :answer/id #uuid "06f58c8d-dd36-54da-a7cb-4e0680dd8d11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284252 :answer-field/choices ["answer-c09c3188-f84e-57d0-8dc1-83f1a60a9756" "answer-d5975ee2-3ecf-500e-8e1c-2962b00ed738" "answer-9967aa49-50aa-5f71-ad63-89982427cb06" "answer-76639164-3dd6-5449-9e16-8c706f2d6c36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c09c3188-f84e-57d0-8dc1-83f1a60a9756" :answer/id #uuid "c09c3188-f84e-57d0-8dc1-83f1a60a9756" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5975ee2-3ecf-500e-8e1c-2962b00ed738" :answer/id #uuid "d5975ee2-3ecf-500e-8e1c-2962b00ed738" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9967aa49-50aa-5f71-ad63-89982427cb06" :answer/id #uuid "9967aa49-50aa-5f71-ad63-89982427cb06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76639164-3dd6-5449-9e16-8c706f2d6c36" :answer/id #uuid "76639164-3dd6-5449-9e16-8c706f2d6c36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186408093 :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0fd2738-95bc-5ce8-af8a-007c2793d79e" "answer-e88bb104-5429-5d48-9b16-2281d5b1fabf" "answer-53357543-e2c9-531c-90c9-df1aa8ac742f" "answer-6e310c38-d0e1-5c20-a7e8-fcc4464b7b54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0fd2738-95bc-5ce8-af8a-007c2793d79e" :answer/id #uuid "f0fd2738-95bc-5ce8-af8a-007c2793d79e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}<1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e88bb104-5429-5d48-9b16-2281d5b1fabf" :answer/id #uuid "e88bb104-5429-5d48-9b16-2281d5b1fabf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}>1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53357543-e2c9-531c-90c9-df1aa8ac742f" :answer/id #uuid "53357543-e2c9-531c-90c9-df1aa8ac742f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}\\ge 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e310c38-d0e1-5c20-a7e8-fcc4464b7b54" :answer/id #uuid "6e310c38-d0e1-5c20-a7e8-fcc4464b7b54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}\\le 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186323801 :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-1 & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =3(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-1) \\\\ (z+1) & =\\pm \\sqrt{3(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the exterior of the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1$, including its boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\ge 1\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186323405 :answer-field/correct "answer-8a7e4314-461a-51dd-8e7e-003b239d4df1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8a23aa13-d540-5d99-be2b-3b822200ad45" "answer-8a7e4314-461a-51dd-8e7e-003b239d4df1" "answer-6d07251a-4f5b-5fe1-a5c8-5c5e4e7f9bfc" "answer-9bc62f3e-4d97-58eb-bb7f-08bb44e41d57"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a23aa13-d540-5d99-be2b-3b822200ad45" :answer/id #uuid "8a23aa13-d540-5d99-be2b-3b822200ad45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}<1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a7e4314-461a-51dd-8e7e-003b239d4df1" :answer/id #uuid "8a7e4314-461a-51dd-8e7e-003b239d4df1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\ge 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d07251a-4f5b-5fe1-a5c8-5c5e4e7f9bfc" :answer/id #uuid "6d07251a-4f5b-5fe1-a5c8-5c5e4e7f9bfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}<0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bc62f3e-4d97-58eb-bb7f-08bb44e41d57" :answer/id #uuid "9bc62f3e-4d97-58eb-bb7f-08bb44e41d57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\ge 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1a64d7fd-d80f-53bd-910a-60419647eb47" :question/id #uuid "1a64d7fd-d80f-53bd-910a-60419647eb47" :question/math-academy-id "q-36323" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the hyperboloid of one sheet $9{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperboloid. This gives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}+8\\cdot {0}^{2}-4{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is the equation of a hyperbola in $xz$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0a302038-8631-5953-a8f8-0cdccc24c035"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0a302038-8631-5953-a8f8-0cdccc24c035" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a302038-8631-5953-a8f8-0cdccc24c035" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7c79725f-53ef-57ae-9875-557218ef53d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ca33020b-9a08-5192-a614-1388ffc83e34" "answer-914100ae-dbbe-52f6-afc8-728db3a0a28f" "answer-2f18a57e-f42f-587e-847b-92b2446cd452" "answer-7c79725f-53ef-57ae-9875-557218ef53d4" "answer-3710bae3-9011-5bcd-9242-2708a46849d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca33020b-9a08-5192-a614-1388ffc83e34" :answer/id #uuid "ca33020b-9a08-5192-a614-1388ffc83e34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-914100ae-dbbe-52f6-afc8-728db3a0a28f" :answer/id #uuid "914100ae-dbbe-52f6-afc8-728db3a0a28f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f18a57e-f42f-587e-847b-92b2446cd452" :answer/id #uuid "2f18a57e-f42f-587e-847b-92b2446cd452" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}=-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c79725f-53ef-57ae-9875-557218ef53d4" :answer/id #uuid "7c79725f-53ef-57ae-9875-557218ef53d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3710bae3-9011-5bcd-9242-2708a46849d8" :answer/id #uuid "3710bae3-9011-5bcd-9242-2708a46849d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059831 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bd9a81c2-dd21-5cb3-9488-a8b270b5ad9b" "question-27716467-fe24-5b2e-a5ee-4be993036021"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bd9a81c2-dd21-5cb3-9488-a8b270b5ad9b" :question/id #uuid "bd9a81c2-dd21-5cb3-9488-a8b270b5ad9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124446" :question/problem "What is $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{245}^{∘}$ expressed in terms of a reference angle?" :question/worked-solution "To express $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{245}^{∘}$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ we follow three steps:\n\n1\\. Find its reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}.$\n\n2\\. Calculate the value of the function for ${\\theta }_{R}.$\n\n3\\. Determine whether the resulting value is positive or negative.\n\nFirst, let's draw the angle ${245}^{∘}$ in the coordinate plane (CAST diagram):\n\n![](images/31/312fc3581d9da413254a0eb4dbc64091b286675492821838ba9a65ee06f45a7c.png)\n\n**Step 1**: Since $\\theta ={245}^{∘}$ is in the $3$rd quadrant, the reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =\\theta -{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={245}^{∘}-{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={65}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: The given ratio is $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{245}^{∘}$, and therefore we're interested in $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{\\theta }_{R}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{65}^{∘}.$\n\n**Step 3:** The ratio $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{245}^{∘}$ must be *negative* because the sine ratio is *always* negative in the $3$rd quadrant. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{245}^{∘}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{65}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-