culate $∇\\times (F+G)$ at the point $(0,-1,1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i+3z\\,j-2y\\,\\text{k},\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=(6z-1)\\,j.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & 3z & -2y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3z)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3z)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)]k \\\\  & =(-2-3)i-(0-0)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =-5\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =-5\\,i+(6z-1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,-1,1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F+G))(0,-1,1) & =-5\\,i+(6(1)-1)\\,j \\\\  & =-5\\,i+5\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-743b8050-afb0-5239-be1f-b571663c2f9a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-743b8050-afb0-5239-be1f-b571663c2f9a" :answer-field/id #uuid "743b8050-afb0-5239-be1f-b571663c2f9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-65367f18-ef71-5d52-84f0-4d352c7adcb5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-65367f18-ef71-5d52-84f0-4d352c7adcb5" "answer-504fe88b-8989-50fd-9bf6-4fb3a0874f14" "answer-de460cf2-dd72-57b6-89cf-2648f5feed59" "answer-953d0060-629d-5930-8b1a-dc079696c8e2" "answer-cb311272-e389-523f-83ba-df596e274f53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65367f18-ef71-5d52-84f0-4d352c7adcb5" :answer/id #uuid "65367f18-ef71-5d52-84f0-4d352c7adcb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\,i+5\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-504fe88b-8989-50fd-9bf6-4fb3a0874f14" :answer/id #uuid "504fe88b-8989-50fd-9bf6-4fb3a0874f14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de460cf2-dd72-57b6-89cf-2648f5feed59" :answer/id #uuid "de460cf2-dd72-57b6-89cf-2648f5feed59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-953d0060-629d-5930-8b1a-dc079696c8e2" :answer/id #uuid "953d0060-629d-5930-8b1a-dc079696c8e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb311272-e389-523f-83ba-df596e274f53" :answer/id #uuid "cb311272-e389-523f-83ba-df596e274f53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,i-j+5\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180186 :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (F+2G)$ at the point $(1,1,1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z\\,i+{x}^{2}y\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z\\,i+(xy-2xyz)\\,j-xz\\,k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+2G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times (2G) \\\\  & =∇\\times F+2∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {x}^{2}z & 0 & {x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(0)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(0)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}z)]k \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-0)i-(2xy-{x}^{2})j+(0-0)k \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\,i+({x}^{2}-2xy)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+2G) & =∇\\times F+2∇\\times G \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\,i+({x}^{2}-2xy)\\,j+2[{x}^{2}z\\,i+(xy-2xyz)\\,j-xz\\,k] \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}z)\\,i+({x}^{2}-2xy+2xy-4xyz)\\,j-2xz\\,k \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(1+2z)\\,i+({x}^{2}-4xyz)\\,j-2xz\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(1,1,1),$ we get\n\n$$\n(∇\\times (F+2G))(1,1,1)=3\\,i-3\\,j-2\\,k.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186178660 :answer-field/correct "answer-ebce6acb-ae41-52f5-ac95-a2a586b9f5fb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0f9b5739-0938-5c65-94b0-f1b4aa69e157" "answer-6a99f0f4-e5ef-5f99-af5c-c942163885d5" "answer-ebce6acb-ae41-52f5-ac95-a2a586b9f5fb" "answer-1067630d-4e4d-554b-9f81-a5561e8e478a" "answer-045f588e-73be-514d-9fd9-46ece75a5e69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f9b5739-0938-5c65-94b0-f1b4aa69e157" :answer/id #uuid "0f9b5739-0938-5c65-94b0-f1b4aa69e157" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i-3\\,j-2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a99f0f4-e5ef-5f99-af5c-c942163885d5" :answer/id #uuid "6a99f0f4-e5ef-5f99-af5c-c942163885d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i-\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebce6acb-ae41-52f5-ac95-a2a586b9f5fb" :answer/id #uuid "ebce6acb-ae41-52f5-ac95-a2a586b9f5fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,i-3\\,j-2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1067630d-4e4d-554b-9f81-a5561e8e478a" :answer/id #uuid "1067630d-4e4d-554b-9f81-a5561e8e478a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,i-4\\,j-4\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-045f588e-73be-514d-9fd9-46ece75a5e69" :answer/id #uuid "045f588e-73be-514d-9fd9-46ece75a5e69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,i-2\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0ea54cb1-a0d4-5539-a164-15702dc537d3" :question/id #uuid "0ea54cb1-a0d4-5539-a164-15702dc537d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-105795" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (F-3G)$ at the point $(1,0,9)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=(2\\sqrt{z}+x)\\,i+xy\\,j+{y}^{2}\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=3{x}^{2}y\\,k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-3G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times (-3G) \\\\  & =∇\\times F-3∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{z}+x & xy & {y}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2\\sqrt{z}+x)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\sqrt{z}+x)]k \\\\  & =(2y-0)i-(0-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}})j+(y-0)k \\\\  & =2y\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,j+y\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-3G) & =∇\\times F-3∇\\times G \\\\  & =2y\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,j+y\\,k-3[3{x}^{2}y\\,k] \\\\  & =2y\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,j+y\\,k-9{x}^{2}y\\,k \\\\  & =2y\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,j+y(1-9{x}^{2})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(1,0,9),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-3G))(1,0,9) & =2(0)\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9}}\\,j+0(1-9(1)^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-523554aa-2a52-5d37-8cc9-84d837bdff76"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-523554aa-2a52-5d37-8cc9-84d837bdff76" :answer-field/id #uuid "523554aa-2a52-5d37-8cc9-84d837bdff76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1029c273-1bc6-53a7-8ba2-8c396398f3e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a6aa9a17-9981-5e03-a5c9-1692e6dae401" "answer-8f4111c9-6604-575a-b3bf-8b514228499e" "answer-a4873e67-7fec-50d7-b791-b5ed499f85ae" "answer-3c1f5b71-a8d9-5bee-8b46-73f0baef7978" "answer-1029c273-1bc6-53a7-8ba2-8c396398f3e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6aa9a17-9981-5e03-a5c9-1692e6dae401" :answer/id #uuid "a6aa9a17-9981-5e03-a5c9-1692e6dae401" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f4111c9-6604-575a-b3bf-8b514228499e" :answer/id #uuid "8f4111c9-6604-575a-b3bf-8b514228499e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-i-\\frac{1}{3}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4873e67-7fec-50d7-b791-b5ed499f85ae" :answer/id #uuid "a4873e67-7fec-50d7-b791-b5ed499f85ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c1f5b71-a8d9-5bee-8b46-73f0baef7978" :answer/id #uuid "3c1f5b71-a8d9-5bee-8b46-73f0baef7978" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,i-3\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1029c273-1bc6-53a7-8ba2-8c396398f3e2" :answer/id #uuid "1029c273-1bc6-53a7-8ba2-8c396398f3e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1adbaf5f-6695-5acc-8c83-a7d990c62422" :question/id #uuid "1adbaf5f-6695-5acc-8c83-a7d990c62422" :question/math-academy-id "q-105964" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨3z,2x,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=xz+y.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,3,2⟩,\\,∇f=⟨z,1,x⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(1,0,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ z & 1 & x \\\\ 3z & 2x & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[1(0)-x(2x)]i-[z(0)-x(3z)]j+[z(2x)-1(3z)]k \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}\\,i+3xz\\,j+(2xz-3z)\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-2{x}^{2},3xz,2xz-3z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(xz+y)⟨0,3,2⟩+⟨-2{x}^{2},3xz,2xz-3z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,3(xz+y),2(xz+y)⟩+⟨-2{x}^{2},3xz,2xz-3z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{x}^{2},3(xz+y)+3xz,2(xz+y)+2xz-3z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{x}^{2},6xz+3y,4xz+2y-3z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(1,0,0) & =⟨-2(1)^{2},6(1)(0)+3(0),4(1)(0)+2(0)-3(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-358ba299-db97-5c30-b480-8ad69e4c1d58"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-358ba299-db97-5c30-b480-8ad69e4c1d58" :answer-field/id #uuid "358ba299-db97-5c30-b480-8ad69e4c1d58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-716825f9-f0c6-5e08-968a-88f84d52da1e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-716825f9-f0c6-5e08-968a-88f84d52da1e" "answer-9b8592fa-9388-57e4-a3b0-75e82fd0fa0b" "answer-b34859f7-1d1a-5aa1-a406-403532f54aee" "answer-0c8eee1c-f133-5076-90a3-abd6303c7686" "answer-3bc83cd3-ee31-5732-a9e3-7f6452fee0f6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-716825f9-f0c6-5e08-968a-88f84d52da1e" :answer/id #uuid "716825f9-f0c6-5e08-968a-88f84d52da1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2,0,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b8592fa-9388-57e4-a3b0-75e82fd0fa0b" :answer/id #uuid "9b8592fa-9388-57e4-a3b0-75e82fd0fa0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,-2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b34859f7-1d1a-5aa1-a406-403532f54aee" :answer/id #uuid "b34859f7-1d1a-5aa1-a406-403532f54aee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c8eee1c-f133-5076-90a3-abd6303c7686" :answer/id #uuid "0c8eee1c-f133-5076-90a3-abd6303c7686" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,3,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3bc83cd3-ee31-5732-a9e3-7f6452fee0f6" :answer/id #uuid "3bc83cd3-ee31-5732-a9e3-7f6452fee0f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,-1,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-38f95650-79fd-557c-9c72-45e47bd9ea35" :question/id #uuid "38f95650-79fd-557c-9c72-45e47bd9ea35" :question/math-academy-id "q-131475" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x{e}^{y},yz,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{-y}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨-y,0,-x{e}^{y}⟩,\\,∇f=⟨{e}^{-y},-x{e}^{-y},0⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(0,1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {e}^{-y} & -x{e}^{-y} & 0 \\\\ x{e}^{y} & yz & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[(-x{e}^{-y})(0)-(yz)(0)]i-[({e}^{-y})(0)-(x{e}^{y})(0)]j+[({e}^{-y})(yz)-(x{e}^{y})(-x{e}^{-y})]k \\\\  & =0\\,i+0j+(yz{e}^{-y}+{x}^{2})k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,yz{e}^{-y}+{x}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(x{e}^{-y})⟨-y,0,-x{e}^{y}⟩+⟨0,0,yz{e}^{-y}+{x}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-xy{e}^{-y},0,-{x}^{2}⟩+⟨0,0,yz{e}^{-y}+{x}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-xy{e}^{-y},0,yz{e}^{-y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)(0,1,2)=⟨0,0,\\frac{2}{e}⟩.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7200c5c6-834c-582d-bb4f-488640d68497"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7200c5c6-834c-582d-bb4f-488640d68497" :answer-field/id #uuid "7200c5c6-834c-582d-bb4f-488640d68497" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8553596b-4bed-5f28-bf3d-359109448203" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8553596b-4bed-5f28-bf3d-359109448203" "answer-c876445d-364d-54c2-a964-eda7f78c0d80" "answer-ef621264-33c3-594b-bcb1-888fe58a6145" "answer-cb2b2a5b-e478-5762-9565-7d86b996e74f" "answer-e39f0bf0-41ab-5680-8a0a-a65746d7ad80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8553596b-4bed-5f28-bf3d-359109448203" :answer/id #uuid "8553596b-4bed-5f28-bf3d-359109448203" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,0,\\frac{2}{e}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c876445d-364d-54c2-a964-eda7f78c0d80" :answer/id #uuid "c876445d-364d-54c2-a964-eda7f78c0d80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,2e,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef621264-33c3-594b-bcb1-888fe58a6145" :answer/id #uuid "ef621264-33c3-594b-bcb1-888fe58a6145" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2e,1,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb2b2a5b-e478-5762-9565-7d86b996e74f" :answer/id #uuid "cb2b2a5b-e478-5762-9565-7d86b996e74f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{e},0,2e⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e39f0bf0-41ab-5680-8a0a-a65746d7ad80" :answer/id #uuid "e39f0bf0-41ab-5680-8a0a-a65746d7ad80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{e},0,\\frac{2}{e}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133885 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f11ffdfd-619b-56d9-be79-9ad5a11a6df9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f11ffdfd-619b-56d9-be79-9ad5a11a6df9" :question/id #uuid "f11ffdfd-619b-56d9-be79-9ad5a11a6df9" :question/math-academy-id "q-109851" :question/problem "Which of the following subspaces must be orthogonal to $\\text{Null}(B)$ for every matrix $B?$\n\nI. $\\text{Null}({B}^{T})$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(B)$\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}({B}^{T})$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Null}(B)$ contains all vectors that, when pre-multiplied by $B,$ result in the zero-vector $0.$ \n\nWhen pre-multiplying a vector by $B,$ we actually multiply each row of $B$ by that vector. So, $\\text{Null}(B)$ must be orthogonal to the row space of $B,$ which is $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"\n\n**Note:** In general, the four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $B$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/18/18713ed3d103ca0a02d74cede1e6448012e0aa28a2df804d41cfb277589a0158.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-24c992c9-8052-5ffe-8e34-a8bb4e14e451"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-24c992c9-8052-5ffe-8e34-a8bb4e14e451" :answer-field/id #uuid "24c992c9-8052-5ffe-8e34-a8bb4e14e451" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7aced2dd-2260-5a76-91a1-48cb49a84605" :answer-field/choices ["answer-768b47d4-ad9c-5a4c-818c-2d77de8a37b0" "answer-fb4475e7-9df7-5f01-8da5-2b4f45ddcbb7" "answer-c36cab80-11fb-53dd-8c1f-1830080636ad" "answer-48b52c8d-5a6d-57b6-b139-de7e62153564" "answer-7aced2dd-2260-5a76-91a1-48cb49a84605"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-768b47d4-ad9c-5a4c-818c-2d77de8a37b0" :answer/id #uuid "768b47d4-ad9c-5a4c-818c-2d77de8a37b0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb4475e7-9df7-5f01-8da5-2b4f45ddcbb7" :answer/id #uuid "fb4475e7-9df7-5f01-8da5-2b4f45ddcbb7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c36cab80-11fb-53dd-8c1f-1830080636ad" :answer/id #uuid "c36cab80-11fb-53dd-8c1f-1830080636ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48b52c8d-5a6d-57b6-b139-de7e62153564" :answer/id #uuid "48b52c8d-5a6d-57b6-b139-de7e62153564" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7aced2dd-2260-5a76-91a1-48cb49a84605" :answer/id #uuid "7aced2dd-2260-5a76-91a1-48cb49a84605" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129253 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-07118ae1-aa98-5cd9-a3cf-0fa1f32e3170" "question-38e88fc8-0fa8-5760-aae8-838a940ddec3" "question-13c802b0-f24f-5ef6-be2f-44ec40da3fdf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129154 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-571594cb-dae3-572c-bed1-7b71f8315ee0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186128972 :question/problem "![](images/d8/d8d6f70aed4d013bfcdd9060124ad003e3e1ed6ce70852e4f60d71cdd8d65cc4.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $x = -1$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n\nII. $x=-3$ and $x=2$ are simple roots.\n\nIII. $p(x)\\to-\\infty$ as $x\\to-\\infty.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129145 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0e919c69-a07f-59d0-9a4f-80f07bde8e75"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186128960 :question/problem "![](images/59/5970275bd70bcfd944c03abc8f60c2b159e3545dc876a0dd05bc23343b85bdec.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the equation of the polynomial above?\n\nI. $y=(x+2)(x+1)^2(x-2)$\n\nII. $y=(x+2)^3(x+1)^2(x-2)$\n\nIII. $y=(x+2)(x+1)^2(x-2)^3$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-07118ae1-aa98-5cd9-a3cf-0fa1f32e3170" :question/id #uuid "07118ae1-aa98-5cd9-a3cf-0fa1f32e3170" :question/math-academy-id "q-141139" :question/problem "![](images/ce/cec773f27259f88a93d2eb396319fc148a68f36311d611193b911cb2ef74162e.png)\n\nA part of the graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is given above. Which of the following statements is true?" :question/worked-solution "| Multiplicity | Sketch | Sketch |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ \n\n (Simple Root) | ![](images/5a/5a0221f93c65a1eeb4503604a558a6da81c4c7af81c2c52cc35ecf3d189fe99f.png) | ![](images/d5/d556b4edf39181eebb7ec87c344d6f657a6875ecd2745405eaf5351ccaff6f96.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Even | ![](images/9d/9d14c2588da2ee9c9f5bbc32a70791146bed609ea0d6d5912aeaa2edab02e2d7.png) | ![](images/28/28ad9248a9a509e3a44937d0438fb2366f550a22360d01b9b6a29bcac41357e8.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Odd | ![](images/3a/3ae81378cb3c918dd5b7730519eb5a91e949f88eef9f03f4910f4ab8fb3cd5a9.png) | ![](images/95/9506a7ce4031f1f6244c0110c3235f66ea5652bb53548a032732869cf21f5997.png) |\n\nIt's possible to determine information regarding the multiplicities of the roots of a polynomial from its graph.\n\n- If the graph intersects the $x$-axis but is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *simple* root $x=a.$\n\n- If the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *multiple* root $x=a.$ Furthermore:\n\n- If the graph touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *even*.\n\n- If the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *odd*.\n\nIn our case, the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=-7.$ Therefore, $x=-7$ is a *simple* root." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7dcda837-822e-5eeb-afa7-533dae64c1d0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7dcda837-822e-5eeb-afa7-533dae64c1d0" :answer-field/id #uuid "7dcda837-822e-5eeb-afa7-533dae64c1d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e630767-5cfc-5240-86dc-1f0035f469b2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-69f96cf3-ab2c-51fc-9b3c-ef729116e639" "answer-fffa4889-a79d-5ffe-a1c5-5d4b141384c5" "answer-4e630767-5cfc-5240-86dc-1f0035f469b2" "answer-ee6a1dc3-31ce-59a1-b68d-705ad5178538" "answer-fb64727d-54cb-5ca3-9501-af15e869cd65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69f96cf3-ab2c-51fc-9b3c-ef729116e639" :answer/id #uuid "69f96cf3-ab2c-51fc-9b3c-ef729116e639" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-7$ is a multiple root of even multiplicity" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fffa4889-a79d-5ffe-a1c5-5d4b141384c5" :answer/id #uuid "fffa4889-a79d-5ffe-a1c5-5d4b141384c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-7$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e630767-5cfc-5240-86dc-1f0035f469b2" :answer/id #uuid "4e630767-5cfc-5240-86dc-1f0035f469b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-7$ is a simple root" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee6a1dc3-31ce-59a1-b68d-705ad5178538" :answer/id #uuid "ee6a1dc3-31ce-59a1-b68d-705ad5178538" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-7$ is a simple root of even multiplicity" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb64727d-54cb-5ca3-9501-af15e869cd65" :answer/id #uuid "fb64727d-54cb-5ca3-9501-af15e869cd65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-7$ is not a root of $p(x)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-38e88fc8-0fa8-5760-aae8-838a940ddec3" :question/id #uuid "38e88fc8-0fa8-5760-aae8-838a940ddec3" :question/math-academy-id "q-141135" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d32c9f722bee1a6391c943335c0024be2237aa1779760013fa368508bc8473b6.png)\n\nA part of the graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is given above. Which of the following statements is true?" :question/worked-solution "| Multiplicity | Sketch | Sketch |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ \n\n (Simple Root) | ![](images/5a/5a0221f93c65a1eeb4503604a558a6da81c4c7af81c2c52cc35ecf3d189fe99f.png) | ![](images/d5/d556b4edf39181eebb7ec87c344d6f657a6875ecd2745405eaf5351ccaff6f96.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Even | ![](images/9d/9d14c2588da2ee9c9f5bbc32a70791146bed609ea0d6d5912aeaa2edab02e2d7.png) | ![](images/28/28ad9248a9a509e3a44937d0438fb2366f550a22360d01b9b6a29bcac41357e8.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Odd | ![](images/3a/3ae81378cb3c918dd5b7730519eb5a91e949f88eef9f03f4910f4ab8fb3cd5a9.png) | ![](images/95/9506a7ce4031f1f6244c0110c3235f66ea5652bb53548a032732869cf21f5997.png) |\n\nIt's possible to determine information regarding the multiplicities of the roots of a polynomial from its graph.\n\n- If the graph intersects the $x$-axis but is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *simple* root $x=a.$\n\n- If the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *multiple* root $x=a.$ Furthermore:\n\n- If the graph touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *even*.\n\n- If the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *odd*.\n\nIn our case, the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=4.$ Therefore, $x=4$ is a *simple* root." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dbff19e8-6bb3-5cf7-9577-3cd5d10ab5e6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dbff19e8-6bb3-5cf7-9577-3cd5d10ab5e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "dbff19e8-6bb3-5cf7-9577-3cd5d10ab5e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3b07e4e3-0c2c-57b8-8a98-da804eea979d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cb07eeaa-73f5-53cd-aafb-f90deb1645fe" "answer-933a91c2-1408-501c-ad55-d8af282b4a13" "answer-3b07e4e3-0c2c-57b8-8a98-da804eea979d" "answer-6db44c5f-20d5-5b85-8ecb-368e4d5cfdd7" "answer-3f8f19cb-60d5-5ba2-bb9c-13be76b60564"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb07eeaa-73f5-53cd-aafb-f90deb1645fe" :answer/id #uuid "cb07eeaa-73f5-53cd-aafb-f90deb1645fe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=4$ is a multiple root of even multiplicity" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-933a91c2-1408-501c-ad55-d8af282b4a13" :answer/id #uuid "933a91c2-1408-501c-ad55-d8af282b4a13" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=4$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b07e4e3-0c2c-57b8-8a98-da804eea979d" :answer/id #uuid "3b07e4e3-0c2c-57b8-8a98-da804eea979d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=4$ is a simple root" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6db44c5f-20d5-5b85-8ecb-368e4d5cfdd7" :answer/id #uuid "6db44c5f-20d5-5b85-8ecb-368e4d5cfdd7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=4$ is a simple root of even multiplicity" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f8f19cb-60d5-5ba2-bb9c-13be76b60564" :answer/id #uuid "3f8f19cb-60d5-5ba2-bb9c-13be76b60564" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=4$ is not a root of $p(x)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-13c802b0-f24f-5ef6-be2f-44ec40da3fdf" :question/id #uuid "13c802b0-f24f-5ef6-be2f-44ec40da3fdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-141143" :question/problem "![](images/67/67c87009cbafcf40172b4de6cae4cb57e37660dd15235f67500c2a0532d42dee.png)\n\nA part of the graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements is true?" :question/worked-solution "| Multiplicity | Sketch | Sketch |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ \n\n (Simple Root) | ![](images/5a/5a0221f93c65a1eeb4503604a558a6da81c4c7af81c2c52cc35ecf3d189fe99f.png) | ![](images/d5/d556b4edf39181eebb7ec87c344d6f657a6875ecd2745405eaf5351ccaff6f96.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Even | ![](images/9d/9d14c2588da2ee9c9f5bbc32a70791146bed609ea0d6d5912aeaa2edab02e2d7.png) | ![](images/28/28ad9248a9a509e3a44937d0438fb2366f550a22360d01b9b6a29bcac41357e8.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Odd | ![](images/3a/3ae81378cb3c918dd5b7730519eb5a91e949f88eef9f03f4910f4ab8fb3cd5a9.png) | ![](images/95/9506a7ce4031f1f6244c0110c3235f66ea5652bb53548a032732869cf21f5997.png) |\n\nIt's possible to determine information regarding the multiplicities of the roots of a polynomial from its graph.\n\n- If the graph intersects the $x$-axis but is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *simple* root $x=a.$\n\n- If the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *multiple* root $x=a.$ Furthermore:\n\n- If the graph touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *even*.\n\n- If the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *odd*.\n\nIn our case, the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=2.$ So, $x=2$ is a *multiple* root. \n\nFurthermore, the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=2.$ So, $x=2$ has *odd* multiplicity.\n\nTherefore, $x=2$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-599c8793-e8c3-5306-b56b-04269b939632"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-599c8793-e8c3-5306-b56b-04269b939632" :answer-field/id #uuid "599c8793-e8c3-5306-b56b-04269b939632" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-73918c51-a1f9-582d-9ee3-270673767b71" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce1f700e-ca83-50c0-a87a-7c914e000acf" "answer-73918c51-a1f9-582d-9ee3-270673767b71" "answer-c8681ab5-0854-580f-a01d-5117b98125ce" "answer-a0ea4cfe-3c2b-531a-b7fa-3167daa6ad38" "answer-bf72962b-ac8f-5b9c-8f14-e9632a0c6017"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce1f700e-ca83-50c0-a87a-7c914e000acf" :answer/id #uuid "ce1f700e-ca83-50c0-a87a-7c914e000acf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ is a multiple root of even multiplicity" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73918c51-a1f9-582d-9ee3-270673767b71" :answer/id #uuid "73918c51-a1f9-582d-9ee3-270673767b71" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8681ab5-0854-580f-a01d-5117b98125ce" :answer/id #uuid "c8681ab5-0854-580f-a01d-5117b98125ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ is a simple root" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0ea4cfe-3c2b-531a-b7fa-3167daa6ad38" :answer/id #uuid "a0ea4cfe-3c2b-531a-b7fa-3167daa6ad38" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ is a simple root of even multiplicity" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf72962b-ac8f-5b9c-8f14-e9632a0c6017" :answer/id #uuid "bf72962b-ac8f-5b9c-8f14-e9632a0c6017" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ is not a root of $p(x)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-571594cb-dae3-572c-bed1-7b71f8315ee0" :question/id #uuid "571594cb-dae3-572c-bed1-7b71f8315ee0" :question/math-academy-id "q-70812" :question/problem "![](images/75/75b9d9a0500f526670c59b4f92c28f4da8d979e39c615ae4f25ec960a80ca1e0.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $x=0$ is a root of odd multiplicity.\n\nII. $x=0$ is a simple root.\n\nIII. $p(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=0$ has an odd multiplicity because at $x=0$ the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The root $x=0$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at that point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement III is true. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $+\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves up in the positive direction towards $+\\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2c25fadf-bd40-53ef-b6e5-84027da47699"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2c25fadf-bd40-53ef-b6e5-84027da47699" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c25fadf-bd40-53ef-b6e5-84027da47699" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d37635de-5c8a-521b-bbfe-c96b155ed7f2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-56626858-9917-5e86-a480-5880f6bda1c5" "answer-d37635de-5c8a-521b-bbfe-c96b155ed7f2" "answer-af6f95ab-c708-5e53-9fff-dc760663af8f" "answer-e37d7018-5d40-5dcd-9b09-15c860e95b89" "answer-377d2e81-b433-5192-b5f2-5e1f0c06f2bd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56626858-9917-5e86-a480-5880f6bda1c5" :answer/id #uuid "56626858-9917-5e86-a480-5880f6bda1c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d37635de-5c8a-521b-bbfe-c96b155ed7f2" :answer/id #uuid "d37635de-5c8a-521b-bbfe-c96b155ed7f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af6f95ab-c708-5e53-9fff-dc760663af8f" :answer/id #uuid "af6f95ab-c708-5e53-9fff-dc760663af8f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e37d7018-5d40-5dcd-9b09-15c860e95b89" :answer/id #uuid "e37d7018-5d40-5dcd-9b09-15c860e95b89" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-377d2e81-b433-5192-b5f2-5e1f0c06f2bd" :answer/id #uuid "377d2e81-b433-5192-b5f2-5e1f0c06f2bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0e919c69-a07f-59d0-9a4f-80f07bde8e75" :question/id #uuid "0e919c69-a07f-59d0-9a4f-80f07bde8e75" :question/math-academy-id "q-38674" :question/problem "![](images/3b/3b22cee7a07af8745945c07bebf63fac213e26dd210b2e41762784fed64a1532.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the equation of the polynomial curve shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that the function has precisely three distinct roots, $x=0,$ $x=1,$ and $x=2.$\n\nBased on the graph, we can make the following conclusions about the multiplicities of the roots:\n\n- Since the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=0,$ this root has even multiplicity.\n\n- Since the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=1,$ this root has even multiplicity.\n\n- Since the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=2,$ this root is a simple root (the multiplicity equals $1$).\n\nFrom the given options, the only possible equation is $y=-5{x}^{2}(x-1)^{2}(x-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-92540022-5b3a-549e-bcbf-092250f5beb2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-92540022-5b3a-549e-bcbf-092250f5beb2" :answer-field/id #uuid "92540022-5b3a-549e-bcbf-092250f5beb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-03a72d79-34ff-583b-9f8b-56a973a8ea21" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5760f119-2844-592e-b4bc-1ffb9056581a" "answer-03a72d79-34ff-583b-9f8b-56a973a8ea21" "answer-c4a8460d-b922-5d90-a177-f59cb8734c1a" "answer-077eb7e5-61fe-5718-b55a-2b30f9c2f3a9" "answer-fb9d9f52-14d2-5d50-9588-0460d9c70c08"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5760f119-2844-592e-b4bc-1ffb9056581a" :answer/id #uuid "5760f119-2844-592e-b4bc-1ffb9056581a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2x(x-1)^{2}(x-2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03a72d79-34ff-583b-9f8b-56a973a8ea21" :answer/id #uuid "03a72d79-34ff-583b-9f8b-56a973a8ea21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-5{x}^{2}(x-1)^{2}(x-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4a8460d-b922-5d90-a177-f59cb8734c1a" :answer/id #uuid "c4a8460d-b922-5d90-a177-f59cb8734c1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-8{x}^{2}(x-1)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-077eb7e5-61fe-5718-b55a-2b30f9c2f3a9" :answer/id #uuid "077eb7e5-61fe-5718-b55a-2b30f9c2f3a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{3}{4}x(x-1)(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb9d9f52-14d2-5d50-9588-0460d9c70c08" :answer/id #uuid "fb9d9f52-14d2-5d50-9588-0460d9c70c08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{7}{3}{x}^{2}(x-1)(x-2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186348372 :question/problem "![](images/1b/1b2f70dda865622ace25db16dfa55c50c746a88ec4bbc34c8560dd0f342a02ac.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=-{x}^{2}(x+1)(x-2)^{2}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129382 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186317393 :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+2}, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ 1, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. Find the value to which the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ converges when $x=-2.$\n\nThe Fourier series converges to {{field-1}} when $x=-2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186402338 :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4, & x\\in [-\\pi ,0] \\\\ -2, & x\\in (0,\\pi )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼1-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{\\pi (2n-1)}sin\\,((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nAt $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}={{field-4}}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-337e89f2-82ac-52e8-be6a-660664b90047" :activity/id #uuid "337e89f2-82ac-52e8-be6a-660664b90047" :activity/title "Convergence of Fourier Series" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050989 :activity/course 17592186046668 :activity/steps ["step-7141cd06-9a82-558c-a809-bca77fef3ca6" "step-d6afee03-ecd6-5b31-9ab1-2b06d2916529" "step-ca77a31b-9bbe-5f96-a63d-62f998a0a04e" "step-3c44db3b-b9d8-594a-8224-424089042e51" "step-556cc400-3d03-5913-86a0-f17b7e74b961"] :activity/first-step "step-7141cd06-9a82-558c-a809-bca77fef3ca6" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-7141cd06-9a82-558c-a809-bca77fef3ca6" :step/id #uuid "7141cd06-9a82-558c-a809-bca77fef3ca6" :step/content 17592186317393 :step/next "step-d6afee03-ecd6-5b31-9ab1-2b06d2916529" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d6afee03-ecd6-5b31-9ab1-2b06d2916529" :step/id #uuid "d6afee03-ecd6-5b31-9ab1-2b06d2916529" :step/content 17592186375031 :step/next "step-ca77a31b-9bbe-5f96-a63d-62f998a0a04e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ca77a31b-9bbe-5f96-a63d-62f998a0a04e" :step/id #uuid "ca77a31b-9bbe-5f96-a63d-62f998a0a04e" :step/content 17592186432958 :step/next "step-3c44db3b-b9d8-594a-8224-424089042e51" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3c44db3b-b9d8-594a-8224-424089042e51" :step/id #uuid "3c44db3b-b9d8-594a-8224-424089042e51" :step/content 17592186420495 :step/next "step-556cc400-3d03-5913-86a0-f17b7e74b961" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-556cc400-3d03-5913-86a0-f17b7e74b961" :step/id #uuid "556cc400-3d03-5913-86a0-f17b7e74b961" :step/content 17592186402338 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192746 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3b73619e-ed22-51ef-83f4-ae6eed9f4cb4" "question-b5942d8a-a361-5a4c-829b-f23ceb66bd8b" "question-29a403df-d998-5649-bdb5-51e39508e73b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3b73619e-ed22-51ef-83f4-ae6eed9f4cb4" :question/id #uuid "3b73619e-ed22-51ef-83f4-ae6eed9f4cb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-101945" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $2x+9>1$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $9$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+9 & >1 \\\\ 2x+9-9 & >1-9 \\\\ 2x+0 & >-8 \\\\ 2x & >-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & >-8 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & >\\frac{-8}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{2}x}{\\cancel{2}} & >\\frac{-8}{2} \\\\ x & >-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution is $x>-4.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c1/c135701f345826b8ae0ba0cc8dab059834a7e7b968bc87067af45a2622d0514c.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9e773230-0903-5269-b1a1-b9793adfcc4f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9e773230-0903-5269-b1a1-b9793adfcc4f" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e773230-0903-5269-b1a1-b9793adfcc4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0e58b6ff-edc7-55bc-805d-79a600da2102" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bbec4801-2f2d-553f-a54e-786297c0a334" "answer-4e3884ea-4a2a-5eb6-895e-670ae4010193" "answer-f6635464-e3de-53fd-86d7-838f43c01046" "answer-88c5d179-5dbf-56db-b432-bc3a1e8123c7" "answer-0e58b6ff-edc7-55bc-805d-79a600da2102"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bbec4801-2f2d-553f-a54e-786297c0a334" :answer/id #uuid "bbec4801-2f2d-553f-a54e-786297c0a334" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/09/09480ce53cf6d8ed90a6280131b1c545566a4c778adb5c25e5f32d2ee3c9802e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e3884ea-4a2a-5eb6-895e-670ae4010193" :answer/id #uuid "4e3884ea-4a2a-5eb6-895e-670ae4010193" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/26/2692d36cd8012c02f2324dfa66898132a48c2b7ff54bc869220b6a50fad6e584.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6635464-e3de-53fd-86d7-838f43c01046" :answer/id #uuid "f6635464-e3de-53fd-86d7-838f43c01046" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/27/270fc71b3bbd905ffe18b443c1a306b160f2c837a675308417d5b0315d88c5be.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88c5d179-5dbf-56db-b432-bc3a1e8123c7" :answer/id #uuid "88c5d179-5dbf-56db-b432-bc3a1e8123c7" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b0/b0b5b503d8aabf9cae17ce26c868e6a382cf1a4091726a5e3c54e563d66af13b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e58b6ff-edc7-55bc-805d-79a600da2102" :answer/id #uuid "0e58b6ff-edc7-55bc-805d-79a600da2102" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/c1/c135701f345826b8ae0ba0cc8dab059834a7e7b968bc87067af45a2622d0514c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b5942d8a-a361-5a4c-829b-f23ceb66bd8b" :question/id #uuid "b5942d8a-a361-5a4c-829b-f23ceb66bd8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-155559" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $5x-3<2$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $3$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-3 & <2 \\\\ 5x-3+3 & <2+3 \\\\ 5x+0 & <5 \\\\ 5x & <5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & <5 \\\\ \\frac{5x}{5} & <\\frac{5}{5} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{5}x}{\\cancel{5}} & <\\frac{5}{5} \\\\ x & <1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution is $x<1.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c1/c1f7c992d9df85434eaf96e5bd9af52f9b6228e42fede6e9d4001e6471c3c239.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c95bc101-3d53-5754-8210-1facc1f0192a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c95bc101-3d53-5754-8210-1facc1f0192a" :answer-field/id #uuid "c95bc101-3d53-5754-8210-1facc1f0192a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0c9a8ec0-0e56-5bfe-a34d-bcc7fb373cda" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8c34c623-d907-5995-baf4-11d638c93028" "answer-06a51e6f-9a3a-58f7-9636-3b246ae5d6e3" "answer-0c9a8ec0-0e56-5bfe-a34d-bcc7fb373cda" "answer-e62c6989-ba87-590f-bc09-16aad7903942" "answer-eab7fa00-aa04-5abb-837c-33d49463d2c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c34c623-d907-5995-baf4-11d638c93028" :answer/id #uuid "8c34c623-d907-5995-baf4-11d638c93028" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/39/39c072d69e558a095c4671f773ef3cdaed2366997a23edd0112c5bcdb22388dc.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06a51e6f-9a3a-58f7-9636-3b246ae5d6e3" :answer/id #uuid "06a51e6f-9a3a-58f7-9636-3b246ae5d6e3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/8c/8cdfe0777a9a7d8a2096bf1903a0ffb79955d63cbb03a03a8e3f7d1702b162bb.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c9a8ec0-0e56-5bfe-a34d-bcc7fb373cda" :answer/id #uuid "0c9a8ec0-0e56-5bfe-a34d-bcc7fb373cda" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/c1/c1f7c992d9df85434eaf96e5bd9af52f9b6228e42fede6e9d4001e6471c3c239.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e62c6989-ba87-590f-bc09-16aad7903942" :answer/id #uuid "e62c6989-ba87-590f-bc09-16aad7903942" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/cd/cdc5f5b4cdcc56e29d02ee94eb5f2e2128299b5de932966fe2c2a7316bb0f75c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eab7fa00-aa04-5abb-837c-33d49463d2c7" :answer/id #uuid "eab7fa00-aa04-5abb-837c-33d49463d2c7" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f8/f8d2f5c3a4c14d802773a171f71b662d5cb926401cf78bacd26f5dd457a584ad.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-29a403df-d998-5649-bdb5-51e39508e73b" :question/id #uuid "29a403df-d998-5649-bdb5-51e39508e73b" :question/math-academy-id "q-155564" :question/problem "Represent the solution of the inequality $2>3x+5$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $5$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & >3x+5 \\\\ 2-5 & >3x+5-5 \\\\ -3 & >3x+0 \\\\ -3 & >3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3 & >3x \\\\ \\frac{-3}{3} & >\\frac{3x}{3} \\\\ \\frac{-3}{3} & >\\frac{\\cancel{3}x}{\\cancel{3}} \\\\ -1 & >x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember, we also need to flip the inequality.\n\n$$\nx<-1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x<-1.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/09/093f2e5ade9371ae84fa09ab6bee24b18930a781aac7a5fd16c3dd35fecae5ab.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-325c91c6-a03a-513d-b5