" :activity/id #uuid "63c09cac-cd45-58a2-abdb-f4b784ae0ed1" :activity/title "Representing Solutions to Inequalities on Number Lines" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048483 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-3a05fa63-c708-578f-b91c-7abfb0babd01" "step-5f1e04f5-1826-5b79-8562-d80e353e4d76" "step-11c0623a-4eac-5e65-ac53-b36aaa6b05b3"] :activity/first-step "step-3a05fa63-c708-578f-b91c-7abfb0babd01" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-3a05fa63-c708-578f-b91c-7abfb0babd01" :step/id #uuid "3a05fa63-c708-578f-b91c-7abfb0babd01" :step/content "question-3b73619e-ed22-51ef-83f4-ae6eed9f4cb4" :step/next "step-5f1e04f5-1826-5b79-8562-d80e353e4d76" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5f1e04f5-1826-5b79-8562-d80e353e4d76" :step/id #uuid "5f1e04f5-1826-5b79-8562-d80e353e4d76" :step/content "question-b5942d8a-a361-5a4c-829b-f23ceb66bd8b" :step/next "step-11c0623a-4eac-5e65-ac53-b36aaa6b05b3" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-11c0623a-4eac-5e65-ac53-b36aaa6b05b3" :step/id #uuid "11c0623a-4eac-5e65-ac53-b36aaa6b05b3" :step/content "question-29a403df-d998-5649-bdb5-51e39508e73b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110727 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-83c46e33-f8bd-5862-a614-a54a16643b82" "question-213ef30b-cee1-556f-a46a-815fdaa45856"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-83c46e33-f8bd-5862-a614-a54a16643b82" :question/id #uuid "83c46e33-f8bd-5862-a614-a54a16643b82" :question/math-academy-id "q-220358" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(2x+k)(x-3k)$ is $x=\\frac{1}{4}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{1}{4},$ we will set our result equal to $\\frac{1}{4}.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=(2x+k)(x-3k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{k}{2}$ and ${x}_{2}=3k.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{k}{2}+3k)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6k-k}{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5k}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{1}{4}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5k}{4} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 5k & =1 \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a7afddcb-dc24-5839-bcf0-80fc718004df"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a7afddcb-dc24-5839-bcf0-80fc718004df" :answer-field/id #uuid "a7afddcb-dc24-5839-bcf0-80fc718004df" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-70b54ca2-ba87-5256-9420-5d2e2bf07f05" :answer-field/choices ["answer-70b54ca2-ba87-5256-9420-5d2e2bf07f05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70b54ca2-ba87-5256-9420-5d2e2bf07f05" :answer/id #uuid "70b54ca2-ba87-5256-9420-5d2e2bf07f05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-213ef30b-cee1-556f-a46a-815fdaa45856" :question/id #uuid "213ef30b-cee1-556f-a46a-815fdaa45856" :question/math-academy-id "q-223693" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(x-5k)(x+7k)$ is $x=4.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=4,$ we will set our result equal to $4.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=(x-5k)(x+7k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=5k$ and ${x}_{2}=-7k.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5k+(-7k)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2k}{2} \\\\  & =-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-k & =4 \\\\ k & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2c736d93-e203-5595-b533-b4a4b0df38aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2c736d93-e203-5595-b533-b4a4b0df38aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c736d93-e203-5595-b533-b4a4b0df38aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8e82e1f4-a267-5040-a3a3-bab230ab5205" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8e82e1f4-a267-5040-a3a3-bab230ab5205"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e82e1f4-a267-5040-a3a3-bab230ab5205" :answer/id #uuid "8e82e1f4-a267-5040-a3a3-bab230ab5205" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-49a9bc74-71fa-5e68-804c-d56430f0f339" :activity/id #uuid "49a9bc74-71fa-5e68-804c-d56430f0f339" :activity/title "The Average of the Roots Formula" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050577 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-fd3f6f6d-c09c-53c9-813a-5ff408b3201c" "step-3f1f4856-598c-59df-bf66-05dde605cabb" "step-dd479361-324f-51c6-bbe1-29ac04309691"] :activity/first-step "step-fd3f6f6d-c09c-53c9-813a-5ff408b3201c" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-fd3f6f6d-c09c-53c9-813a-5ff408b3201c" :step/id #uuid "fd3f6f6d-c09c-53c9-813a-5ff408b3201c" :step/content 17592186563746 :step/next "step-3f1f4856-598c-59df-bf66-05dde605cabb" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3f1f4856-598c-59df-bf66-05dde605cabb" :step/id #uuid "3f1f4856-598c-59df-bf66-05dde605cabb" :step/content "question-83c46e33-f8bd-5862-a614-a54a16643b82" :step/next "step-dd479361-324f-51c6-bbe1-29ac04309691" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-dd479361-324f-51c6-bbe1-29ac04309691" :step/id #uuid "dd479361-324f-51c6-bbe1-29ac04309691" :step/content "question-213ef30b-cee1-556f-a46a-815fdaa45856" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124477 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-29b4d870-1dc8-5b15-b7e0-9a157e214c86" "question-389b06ef-bd0c-5b5c-b775-c400f3aed0c2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124478 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-75f69126-c110-5545-9efd-4ceeba235a0c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-29b4d870-1dc8-5b15-b7e0-9a157e214c86" :question/id #uuid "29b4d870-1dc8-5b15-b7e0-9a157e214c86" :question/math-academy-id "q-73605" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $B?$\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-071abeb6-b166-58f5-98b9-047a56887f09"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-071abeb6-b166-58f5-98b9-047a56887f09" :answer-field/id #uuid "071abeb6-b166-58f5-98b9-047a56887f09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ad262205-ce1f-5784-abf9-0b421298aba5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7657acbc-7f7c-5baa-a900-65a74791d07e" "answer-28592cef-ef21-550a-af03-88ded5116553" "answer-ce5d1621-6704-561c-9037-9d2a059c4145" "answer-36c481a9-c678-52df-af3c-ea2c5f3761cb" "answer-ad262205-ce1f-5784-abf9-0b421298aba5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7657acbc-7f7c-5baa-a900-65a74791d07e" :answer/id #uuid "7657acbc-7f7c-5baa-a900-65a74791d07e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st and $3$rd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28592cef-ef21-550a-af03-88ded5116553" :answer/id #uuid "28592cef-ef21-550a-a