 $x$ increases on $[1,3]$, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=140-4{x}^{2}-6{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[3,4].$\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/4a/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=140-4{x}_{i}^{2}-6{y}_{j}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(140-4{x}_{i}^{2}-6{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $140-4{x}_{i}^{2}-6{y}_{j}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f9154569-4f80-5022-95a7-7098388b2e9a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f9154569-4f80-5022-95a7-7098388b2e9a" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9154569-4f80-5022-95a7-7098388b2e9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-41ed938d-77ee-5be4-a56d-de4bd69bddb9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-31bfc5d5-9f9d-5213-931c-1b3cd02fb888" "answer-ad661e93-6e42-58a4-8673-27440b12beb6" "answer-41ed938d-77ee-5be4-a56d-de4bd69bddb9" "answer-a19c395e-1701-5ff5-aa4f-cd31cb0e7730" "answer-2e0c059b-fc3d-53e7-8061-304da24d4444"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31bfc5d5-9f9d-5213-931c-1b3cd02fb888" :answer/id #uuid "31bfc5d5-9f9d-5213-931c-1b3cd02fb888" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "140-4{x}_{i-1}^{2}-6{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad661e93-6e42-58a4-8673-27440b12beb6" :answer/id #uuid "ad661e93-6e42-58a4-8673-27440b12beb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "140-4{x}_{i}^{2}-6{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41ed938d-77ee-5be4-a56d-de4bd69bddb9" :answer/id #uuid "41ed938d-77ee-5be4-a56d-de4bd69bddb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "140-4{x}_{i}^{2}-6{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a19c395e-1701-5ff5-aa4f-cd31cb0e7730" :answer/id #uuid "a19c395e-1701-5ff5-aa4f-cd31cb0e7730" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}^{2}+4{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e0c059b-fc3d-53e7-8061-304da24d4444" :answer/id #uuid "2e0c059b-fc3d-53e7-8061-304da24d4444" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}_{i}^{2}+4{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-00814162-4a3c-58fe-a969-f047df1ff44b" :question/id #uuid "00814162-4a3c-58fe-a969-f047df1ff44b" :question/math-academy-id "q-123512" :question/problem "Let $R=[4,5]\\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=8x-2y-1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=8x-2y-1$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=8x-2y-1$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/a4/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j}-1)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j}-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7dd5fb4c-de84-5f5b-af1b-04ba173b4cb6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7dd5fb4c-de84-5f5b-af1b-04ba173b4cb6" :answer-field/id #uuid "7dd5fb4c-de84-5f5b-af1b-04ba173b4cb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a3864f75-0cfa-59ee-a726-e7e8ad8d3439" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e64185c1-2e85-5ae8-b2eb-1ae0233f3132" "answer-cdbdc0e2-46d4-5cd9-88d6-e3a3f8868846" "answer-d738dade-ca06-5815-b4cf-c20bc75911a5" "answer-a3864f75-0cfa-59ee-a726-e7e8ad8d3439" "answer-f4ad7e6e-60bf-5f8b-97ed-47393ce42054"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e64185c1-2e85-5ae8-b2eb-1ae0233f3132" :answer/id #uuid "e64185c1-2e85-5ae8-b2eb-1ae0233f3132" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}+3{y}_{j}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdbdc0e2-46d4-5cd9-88d6-e3a3f8868846" :answer/id #uuid "cdbdc0e2-46d4-5cd9-88d6-e3a3f8868846" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{i}+3{y}_{j-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d738dade-ca06-5815-b4cf-c20bc75911a5" :answer/id #uuid "d738dade-ca06-5815-b4cf-c20bc75911a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j-1}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3864f75-0cfa-59ee-a726-e7e8ad8d3439" :answer/id #uuid "a3864f75-0cfa-59ee-a726-e7e8ad8d3439" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4ad7e6e-60bf-5f8b-97ed-47393ce42054" :answer/id #uuid "f4ad7e6e-60bf-5f8b-97ed-47393ce42054" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{x}_{i}-2{y}_{j-1}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152720 :question/problem "Let $R=[0,1]\\times [0,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=2x-9y+11.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x-9y+11$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x-9y+11$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/a4/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=2{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j}+11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j}+11)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $2{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j}+11.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186150827 :answer-field/correct "answer-16ab19eb-c13e-5bb3-a2ef-1afd5e349e24" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0e0cd406-85dd-5bc4-bd5d-685e9496f13c" "answer-16ab19eb-c13e-5bb3-a2ef-1afd5e349e24" "answer-7719ca65-9e69-5f3b-a468-5887563f2064" "answer-eef35584-f5cb-5372-a9f4-bbeda99ab63c" "answer-b17ddf68-2aa0-5697-86de-b94206d18053"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e0cd406-85dd-5bc4-bd5d-685e9496f13c" :answer/id #uuid "0e0cd406-85dd-5bc4-bd5d-685e9496f13c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j-1}+11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16ab19eb-c13e-5bb3-a2ef-1afd5e349e24" :answer/id #uuid "16ab19eb-c13e-5bb3-a2ef-1afd5e349e24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j}+11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7719ca65-9e69-5f3b-a468-5887563f2064" :answer/id #uuid "7719ca65-9e69-5f3b-a468-5887563f2064" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{i}-9{y}_{j-1}+11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eef35584-f5cb-5372-a9f4-bbeda99ab63c" :answer/id #uuid "eef35584-f5cb-5372-a9f4-bbeda99ab63c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{i}-9{y}_{j}+11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b17ddf68-2aa0-5697-86de-b94206d18053" :answer/id #uuid "b17ddf68-2aa0-5697-86de-b94206d18053" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}+11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186181075 :answer-field/choices 17592186181076] [:db/retract 17592186181075 :answer-field/choices 17592186181077] [:db/retract 17592186181075 :answer-field/choices 17592186181078] [:db/retract 17592186181075 :answer-field/choices 17592186181079] [:db/retract 17592186181075 :answer-field/choices 17592186181080] [:db/retract 17592186181087 :answer-field/choices 17592186181088] [:db/retract 17592186181087 :answer-field/choices 17592186181089] [:db/retract 17592186181087 :answer-field/choices 17592186181090] [:db/retract 17592186181087 :answer-field/choices 17592186181091] [:db/retract 17592186181087 :answer-field/choices 17592186181092] {:db/id 17592186184211 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-71c17160-e343-5b78-8eee-e55ba4967a40" "question-bb8a5938-134a-51c9-838d-3e4010a8ca50" "question-e52c4055-fdc4-580f-9736-b9940edca056"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184322 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-52455c8c-f427-542e-9cf2-e8b407fdf74f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184323 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6fcb379b-2e62-54ea-ab65-5d0b75f0dbcd" "question-a3f44aac-b56c-541f-849d-0822403501d2" "question-5eff477c-d77b-5edc-9e57-fb4474642e96"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184212 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d53c2052-a67a-5988-8f1a-4c9a720c7a75" "question-71daf213-45ae-576f-97ae-9ffbff2f758a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-71c17160-e343-5b78-8eee-e55ba4967a40" :question/id #uuid "71c17160-e343-5b78-8eee-e55ba4967a40" :question/math-academy-id "q-140322" :question/problem "Rewrite $-({x}^{2}-12x+35)$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "We begin by completing the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-12x+35\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+35\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${6}^{2},$ writing the constant term $35$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2}}_{⏟}-{6}^{2}+35\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-6)^{2}-{6}^{2}+35\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x-6)^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({x}^{2}-12x+35) & =-({(x-6)}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =-{(x-6)}^{2}+1 \\\\  & =1-(x-6)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0e21de81-a1b0-5b51-8bf2-2764e594128c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0e21de81-a1b0-5b51-8bf2-2764e594128c" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e21de81-a1b0-5b51-8bf2-2764e594128c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-12fd1b63-f3c4-5f58-9b24-c3b8e327902e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b7dc3995-7e49-5218-bd7f-84bc849ae212" "answer-ab8f5a47-f218-5790-b0cf-2c6bd714ec14" "answer-12fd1b63-f3c4-5f58-9b24-c3b8e327902e" "answer-f44e234d-afc4-503a-ae90-2371906eb7fb" "answer-2def7528-a392-5c38-a317-849706e41d62"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7dc3995-7e49-5218-bd7f-84bc849ae212" :answer/id #uuid "b7dc3995-7e49-5218-bd7f-84bc849ae212" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1-(x+6)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab8f5a47-f218-5790-b0cf-2c6bd714ec14" :answer/id #uuid "ab8f5a47-f218-5790-b0cf-2c6bd714ec14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-36-(x-6)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12fd1b63-f3c4-5f58-9b24-c3b8e327902e" :answer/id #uuid "12fd1b63-f3c4-5f58-9b24-c3b8e327902e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-(x-6)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f44e234d-afc4-503a-ae90-2371906eb7fb" :answer/id #uuid "f44e234d-afc4-503a-ae90-2371906eb7fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35-(x+6)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2def7528-a392-5c38-a317-849706e41d62" :answer/id #uuid "2def7528-a392-5c38-a317-849706e41d62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "71-(x-6)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bb8a5938-134a-51c9-838d-3e4010a8ca50" :question/id #uuid "bb8a5938-134a-51c9-838d-3e4010a8ca50" :question/math-academy-id "q-140319" :question/problem "Rewrite $-({y}^{2}-8y+60)$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "We begin by completing the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-8y+60\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 4y+60\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${4}^{2},$ writing the constant term $60$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 4y+{4}^{2}}_{⏟}-{4}^{2}+60\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(y-4)^{2}-{4}^{2}+60\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(y-4)^{2}+44.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({y}^{2}-8y+60) & =-({(y-4)}^{2}+44) \\\\  & =-{(y-4)}^{2}-44 \\\\  & =-44-(y-4)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f3ff7a4b-bfcf-57eb-b578-4dd542e44b32"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f3ff7a4b-bfcf-57eb-b578-4dd542e44b32" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3ff7a4b-bfcf-57eb-b578-4dd542e44b32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b2f33409-e27b-5ceb-ba94-f59981011277" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b2f33409-e27b-5ceb-ba94-f59981011277" "answer-4b141f66-de8e-506c-a57a-d99a3a23fc93" "answer-3662e5af-46a7-5722-9ccd-5d2228b374fe" "answer-ec3c2400-2c72-5f8d-b4b6-ba5f48a46492" "answer-354b6c4f-e84d-5b59-96f6-ec5ff4ca3b16"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2f33409-e27b-5ceb-ba94-f59981011277" :answer/id #uuid "b2f33409-e27b-5ceb-ba94-f59981011277" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-44-(y-4)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b141f66-de8e-506c-a57a-d99a3a23fc93" :answer/id #uuid "4b141f66-de8e-506c-a57a-d99a3a23fc93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-76-(y+4)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3662e5af-46a7-5722-9ccd-5d2228b374fe" :answer/id #uuid "3662e5af-46a7-5722-9ccd-5d2228b374fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16-(y-4)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec3c2400-2c72-5f8d-b4b6-ba5f48a46492" :answer/id #uuid "ec3c2400-2c72-5f8d-b4b6-ba5f48a46492" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4-(y+4)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-354b6c4f-e84d-5b59-96f6-ec5ff4ca3b16" :answer/id #uuid "354b6c4f-e84d-5b59-96f6-ec5ff4ca3b16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60-(y-4)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e52c4055-fdc4-580f-9736-b9940edca056" :question/id #uuid "e52c4055-fdc4-580f-9736-b9940edca056" :question/math-academy-id "q-25252" :question/problem "Rewrite $-{a}^{2}-10a+16$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-1.$ So, we take out a factor of $-1$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-({a}^{2}+10a-16)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{a}^{2}+10a-16\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{a}^{2}+2\\cdot 5a-16\n$$\n\nThen, we add and then subtract ${5}^{2},$ writing the constant term $16$ last:\n\n$$\n{{a}^{2}+2\\cdot 5a+{5}^{2}}_{⏟}-{5}^{2}-16\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(a+5)^{2}-{5}^{2}-16\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(a+5)^{2}-41\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16-10a-{a}^{2} & =-((a+5)^{2}-41) \\\\  & =-(a+5)^{2}+41 \\\\  & =41-(a+5)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-109e1a5c-722e-5d5b-b384-b35a60da59b9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-109e1a5c-722e-5d5b-b384-b35a60da59b9" :answer-field/id #uuid "109e1a5c-722e-5d5b-b384-b35a60da59b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-20d0d9be-3816-5756-9034-3199caae3743" :answer-field/choices ["answer-11fa85ec-5f23-5583-a1e2-3b339c957d2a" "answer-dbffa828-6ec7-5c64-9988-48bed410abc3" "answer-b6d26802-0604-5ec9-a6dd-63413f57143a" "answer-20d0d9be-3816-5756-9034-3199caae3743" "answer-6f8b8549-d167-5182-a05e-094b9fd3a421"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11fa85ec-5f23-5583-a1e2-3b339c957d2a" :answer/id #uuid "11fa85ec-5f23-5583-a1e2-3b339c957d2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-25-(a+5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dbffa828-6ec7-5c64-9988-48bed410abc3" :answer/id #uuid "dbffa828-6ec7-5c64-9988-48bed410abc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16-(a+5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6d26802-0604-5ec9-a6dd-63413f57143a" :answer/id #uuid "b6d26802-0604-5ec9-a6dd-63413f57143a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25-(a-5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20d0d9be-3816-5756-9034-3199caae3743" :answer/id #uuid "20d0d9be-3816-5756-9034-3199caae3743" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "41-(a+5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f8b8549-d167-5182-a05e-094b9fd3a421" :answer/id #uuid "6f8b8549-d167-5182-a05e-094b9fd3a421" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9-(a-5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184483 :question/problem "Rewrite $-({y}^{2}-5y+6)$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "We begin by completing the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-5y+6\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}y+6\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $6$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}y+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+6\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+6\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({y}^{2}-5y+6) & =-({(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186181075 :answer-field/correct "answer-0d6b0b59-5f4d-58eb-aec7-42d212af1618" :answer-field/choices ["answer-91d492cf-1c56-56df-bd04-4aabaf69aec4" "answer-0d6b0b59-5f4d-58eb-aec7-42d212af1618" "answer-6969fc79-b38b-551a-bfdf-07495efdaf43" "answer-fc78b4ea-4ddc-5ed1-8637-95f6e755fa4c" "answer-0710913b-7399-5b9e-a5a9-f4627344dd74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91d492cf-1c56-56df-bd04-4aabaf69aec4" :answer/id #uuid "91d492cf-1c56-56df-bd04-4aabaf69aec4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31-{(y+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d6b0b59-5f4d-58eb-aec7-42d212af1618" :answer/id #uuid "0d6b0b59-5f4d-58eb-aec7-42d212af1618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6969fc79-b38b-551a-bfdf-07495efdaf43" :answer/id #uuid "6969fc79-b38b-551a-bfdf-07495efdaf43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc78b4ea-4ddc-5ed1-8637-95f6e755fa4c" :answer/id #uuid "fc78b4ea-4ddc-5ed1-8637-95f6e755fa4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{49}{4}-{(y+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0710913b-7399-5b9e-a5a9-f4627344dd74" :answer/id #uuid "0710913b-7399-5b9e-a5a9-f4627344dd74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-52455c8c-f427-542e-9cf2-e8b407fdf74f" :question/id #uuid "52455c8c-f427-542e-9cf2-e8b407fdf74f" :question/math-academy-id "q-140407" :question/problem "Rewrite $-{y}^{2}+9y-21$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-1.$ So, we take out a factor of $-1$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-({y}^{2}-9y+21)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-9y+21\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}y+21\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $21$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}y+{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+21\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+21\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{y}^{2}+9y-21 & =-({(y-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}-{(y-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-416ac210-0c5c-5b57-b96d-e01801ddf600"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-416ac210-0c5c-