p/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186102776 :answer-field/choices 17592186102777] [:db/retract 17592186102776 :answer-field/choices 17592186102778] [:db/retract 17592186102776 :answer-field/choices 17592186102779] [:db/retract 17592186102776 :answer-field/choices 17592186102780] {:db/id 17592186105747 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c" "question-d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c" :question/id #uuid "209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c" :question/math-academy-id "q-37776" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form. The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+3z=-2 \\\\ 0x+y-6z=2 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+3z=-2 \\\\ y-6z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-6z=2\\,⇒\\,y=6z+2\n$$\n\nand substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx-2(6z+2)+3z=-2\\,⇒\\,x=9z+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=9z+2 \\\\ y=6z+2 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9z+2 \\\\ 6z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb" :answer-field/id #uuid "199faf22-a58d-5be8-ae85-92e9998ec1eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b5ff932b-91b7-57e6-b16b-a366e1c519fe" "answer-e497dc2b-a128-5475-b933-f47ae9c3f6d6" "answer-e2c1cc71-f07e-5d4a-8bea-58ef3438d796" "answer-ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937" "answer-a07a72f2-9804-50d0-93ad-1aef75748466"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5ff932b-91b7-57e6-b16b-a366e1c519fe" :answer/id #uuid "b5ff932b-91b7-57e6-b16b-a366e1c519fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9z+2 \\\\ -6z-2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e497dc2b-a128-5475-b933-f47ae9c3f6d6" :answer/id #uuid "e497dc2b-a128-5475-b933-f47ae9c3f6d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9z-2 \\\\ 6z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2c1cc71-f07e-5d4a-8bea-58ef3438d796" :answer/id #uuid "e2c1cc71-f07e-5d4a-8bea-58ef3438d796" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6z+2 \\\\ 9z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937" :answer/id #uuid "ceb29b44-0219-51d7-9c84-59d23212a937" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9z+2 \\\\ 6z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a07a72f2-9804-50d0-93ad-1aef75748466" :answer/id #uuid "a07a72f2-9804-50d0-93ad-1aef75748466" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186106150 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form. The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y-z=1 \\\\ 0x+y+3z=2 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z=1 \\\\ y+3z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3z=2\\,⇒\\,y=2-3z\n$$\n\nand from the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx-z=1\\,⇒\\,x=1+z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=1+z \\\\ y=2-3z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+z \\\\ 2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186102776 :answer-field/correct "answer-c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-93a91dfd-17d2-56d8-8eec-c36565a5f78c" "answer-e977f005-547c-5834-a641-8ed9ae0805ff" "answer-360636f3-e809-5ab4-9cc6-cec1e4085529" "answer-c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93a91dfd-17d2-56d8-8eec-c36565a5f78c" :answer/id #uuid "93a91dfd-17d2-56d8-8eec-c36565a5f78c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1+z \\\\ 2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e977f005-547c-5834-a641-8ed9ae0805ff" :answer/id #uuid "e977f005-547c-5834-a641-8ed9ae0805ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+z \\\\ -2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-360636f3-e809-5ab4-9cc6-cec1e4085529" :answer/id #uuid "360636f3-e809-5ab4-9cc6-cec1e4085529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+z \\\\ 2+3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0" :answer/id #uuid "c453ff5b-68c3-5920-aed9-e4ad1181f6d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+z \\\\ 2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f" :question/id #uuid "d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-131487" :question/problem "Consider the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-8 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for the system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42" :answer-field/id #uuid "df0bd3d6-3a54-5a50-a24f-5924751c2a42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-33eeedd3-31ea-5fb8-bda4-613ebc71cb4b" "answer-25a9ae28-1a32-5418-8561-4a883dda7c79" "answer-820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d" "answer-56d42a9a-e252-5097-8a5e-5d770b1283b2" "answer-2e84c38f-7c51-557b-bdc5-06fc21fc7395"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33eeedd3-31ea-5fb8-bda4-613ebc71cb4b" :answer/id #uuid "33eeedd3-31ea-5fb8-bda4-613ebc71cb4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25a9ae28-1a32-5418-8561-4a883dda7c79" :answer/id #uuid "25a9ae28-1a32-5418-8561-4a883dda7c79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d" :answer/id #uuid "820afba4-be27-5ed0-aa9f-e98ebfbb449d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56d42a9a-e252-5097-8a5e-5d770b1283b2" :answer/id #uuid "56d42a9a-e252-5097-8a5e-5d770b1283b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e84c38f-7c51-557b-bdc5-06fc21fc7395" :answer/id #uuid "2e84c38f-7c51-557b-bdc5-06fc21fc7395" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105748 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae" :question/id #uuid "6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae" :question/math-academy-id "q-73916" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -12 & -20 & -24 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -12 & -20 & -24 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y-5z=-6 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\nx-3y-5z=-6\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=-6+3y+5z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-6+3y+5z \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y,z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6+3y+5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb" :answer-field/id #uuid "41887196-a674-543e-bbae-cd560d625ecb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-21644e7f-62e6-5248-8fde-642e0c0de342" "answer-2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d" "answer-17107aec-addf-5804-8ec0-cfdc83019a95" "answer-7229c467-9034-5d48-a83c-85311714e276" "answer-b593c663-a6cc-5000-bba0-66c693390e09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21644e7f-62e6-5248-8fde-642e0c0de342" :answer/id #uuid "21644e7f-62e6-5248-8fde-642e0c0de342" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3+6y-5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d" :answer/id #uuid "2ce516e8-b614-576d-abdf-2f218226c38d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6+3y+5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17107aec-addf-5804-8ec0-cfdc83019a95" :answer/id #uuid "17107aec-addf-5804-8ec0-cfdc83019a95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6+5y+3z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7229c467-9034-5d48-a83c-85311714e276" :answer/id #uuid "7229c467-9034-5d48-a83c-85311714e276" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6-3y+5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b593c663-a6cc-5000-bba0-66c693390e09" :answer/id #uuid "b593c663-a6cc-5000-bba0-66c693390e09" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105809 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee" :question/id #uuid "70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee" :question/math-academy-id "q-131507" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7x+8y-7z=5 \\\\ 0x-5y+9z=-8 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=1,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3d2924ea-cb37-573b-8ed5-db9237b1f0eb" "answer-66090f14-f9e9-5641-a4c0-de38716a5b27" "answer-b436bc9a-d03e-54a0-b89f-ec3b0cd72d41" "answer-4613befc-1125-5164-88f6-2c0f0d69b67f" "answer-b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d2924ea-cb37-573b-8ed5-db9237b1f0eb" :answer/id #uuid "3d2924ea-cb37-573b-8ed5-db9237b1f0eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66090f14-f9e9-5641-a4c0-de38716a5b27" :answer/id #uuid "66090f14-f9e9-5641-a4c0-de38716a5b27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b436bc9a-d03e-54a0-b89f-ec3b0cd72d41" :answer/id #uuid "b436bc9a-d03e-54a0-b89f-ec3b0cd72d41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4613befc-1125-5164-88f6-2c0f0d69b67f" :answer/id #uuid "4613befc-1125-5164-88f6-2c0f0d69b67f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c" :answer/id #uuid "b98b8374-0faa-5eb1-973d-e09f895dcb8c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186107082 :tutorial/content "Let's consider a system of linear equations where the corresponding coefficient matrix is singular. For example, consider the following system and its associated augmented matrix:\n![](images/1a/1ac826685473beeb7a7c0ee90465db019d0d5b70b1af562aa3469ae4f0a54007.svg)\n\nTo solve the system, we can reduce $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as usual. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -6 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -6 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](images/17/176e4c49ef19bb92d63190dc6674b66ee55b2fdb306293bae65b7f2b2935701d.svg)\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n![](images/a9/a9dd77f0f2ac0f7bd04b5e70fdca3b126d4eb34b0c929caca48c60f138bc644d.svg)\n\nThe **basic variables** are the variables of our system whose coefficients are the pivots of the row echelon form matrix. Let's illustrate the pivots of $M\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/1b/1b776faa6c69553ce04fbddc4e1aa45e18d7390a32ce34d9e0317b2fa83b8752.svg)\n\nThe pivots are\n\n- $m_{11}=1,$ which is the coefficient of $x,$ and\n\n- $m_{22}=1,$ which is the coefficient of $y.$\n\nTherefore, the basic variables are $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe remaining variables are called the **free variables**. We have only one free variable in our system, which is $z$.\n\nFinally, we can describe the **general solution** by finding equations for the basic variables in terms of the free variables. In our case, this means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z$.\n\nTo do this, we apply the back substitution. From the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\ny - 3z = -5\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = -5+3z.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-5+3z)+z=2\\,⟹\\, & x=-3+2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n![](images/e2/e21bb2b83534152d6bf3d1c43efbd301b42717b975f1f9ebaa28ee4bc3ef31bd.svg)\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n![](images/de/de7a613bbbde25e555608ebc419106701d47875e238832eab7533bf87b0f1ce8.svg)\n\nGeometrically, this is the vector equation of a line, and any point on the line is a solution to our original system.\n\nIf we want to find some **particular solution** of the system, we simply choose some particular value of $z$ and find the corresponding values of $x$ and $y$ on the line. For example, if we choose $z=0,$ then the corresponding values are $x=-3$ and $y=-5$ and the particular solution is $x=-3,$ $y=-5,$ $z=0.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129290 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f7c6f3ba-6533-5a1f-b464-492440ca8f6d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f7c6f3ba-6533-5a1f-b464-492440ca8f6d" :question/id #uuid "f7c6f3ba-6533-5a1f-b464-492440ca8f6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-163179" :question/problem "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}$\nand has mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=y,$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters.\nGiven that the center of mass is at $(1,2),$ find the moment of inertia about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =x{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass $(1,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{¯}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{¯}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}((x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}((x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2})y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-1)^{2}y+{y}^{3}-4{y}^{2}+4y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}-\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}+2{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{9}{2}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{9}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}(x-1)^{3}+\\frac{9}{4}x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{9}{2}-(-\\frac{3}{2}+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}+\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bb17ec4b-63ee-5206-af27-3498015a3fd6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bb17ec4b-63ee-5206-af27-3498015a3fd6" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb17ec4b-63ee-5206-af27-3498015a3fd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-82e0bdf4-a937-5979-9022-49f3096a8334" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1d9be715-36a9-5f87-aaff-b73f3c392482" "answer-82e0bdf4-a937-5979-9022-49f3096a8334" "answer-64fb7564-0e54-5edc-bf06-22fc601176e2" "answer-7625faaf-7a06-5f8d-9f7a-5f31afa9fee7" "answer-d5496e58-5442-54c8-8ae7-8fd4a6dda1d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d9be715-36a9-5f87-aaff-b73f3c392482" :answer/id #uuid "1d9be715-36a9-5f87-aaff-b73f3c392482" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82e0bdf4-a937-5979-9022-49f3096a8334" :answer/id #uuid "82e0bdf4-a937-5979-9022-49f3096a8334" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64fb7564-0e54-5edc-bf06-22fc601176e2" :answer/id #uuid "64fb7564-0e54-5edc-bf06-22fc601176e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7625faaf-7a06-5f8d-9f7a-5f31afa9fee7" :answer/id #uuid "7625faaf-7a06-5f8d-9f7a-5f31afa9fee7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5496e58-5442-54c8-8ae7-8fd4a6dda1d3" :answer/id #uuid "d5496e58-5442-54c8-8ae7-8fd4a6dda1d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b45be7aa-3389-5d04-be7f-6c12e62bd7a0" :activity/id #uuid "b45be7aa-3389-5d04-be7f-6c12e62bd7a0" :activity/title "Quiz 5" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046668 :activity/steps ["step-6473ded1-3ff1-56db-b8af-a5723874b273" "step-f1dde27c-6d1b-5b88-844c-736e84bed360" "step-a60b997e-1b94-5fa6-9acb-4e89ec821663" "step-abc6980e-2066-5e2f-89bf-6eb7df162872"] :activity/first-step "step-6473ded1-3ff1-56db-b8af-a5723874b273" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-6473ded1-3ff1-56db-b8af-a5723874b273" :step/id #uuid "6473ded1-3ff1-56db-b8af-a5723874b273" :step/content 17592186360483 :step/next "step-f1dde27c-6d1b-5b88-844c-736e84bed360" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f1dde27c-6d1b-5b88-844c-736e84bed360" :step/id #uuid "f1dde27c-6d1b-5b88-844c-736e84bed360" :step/content "question-f7c6f3ba-6533-5a1f-b464-492440ca8f6d" :step/next "step-a60b997e-1b94-5fa6-9acb-4e89ec821663" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a60b997e-1b94-5fa6-9acb-4e89ec821663" :step/id #uuid "a60b997e-1b94-5fa6-9acb-4e89ec821663" :step/content 17592186199007 :step/next "step-abc6980e-2066-5e2f-89bf-6eb7df162872" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-abc6980e-2066-5e2f-89bf-6eb7df162872" :step/id #uuid "abc6980e-2066-5e2f-89bf-6eb7df162872" :step/content 17592186447158 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147616 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bcd25659-0e9d-5735-91bb-5b7182253798" "question-7f868203-0afb-5c74-9f79-f3b6b4ea5865"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147619 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-533214ac-e847-5fb2-8a57-a2469ce2936c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147297 :question/problem "![](images/f2/f233556f9055563f3956eea7eaf9744fb20993084f4c3eeb5e2e35d730d8d2aa.png)\n\n \n\nWhich of the nets above is the net of a rectangular prism?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/5f/5fc1630e4e44bf68f833004ab975e406b8734fe062849484165310e093d14155.png)\n\n \n\nIf we were to fold the net above along its edges, then we'd get a rectangular prism, as shown below: \n\n![](images/c2/c2f6985ca8cd95a71409936ede80c6f257e863bd459fe5a27178a04ea3edb88c.png)\n\n  \n\nNotice that the other two nets have triangular faces, so they cannot be the nets of a rectangular prism. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147620 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ff018c25-43d3-5a1d-9dbc-90c62eb5eb4d" "question-95eb11a1-9c88-5c12-9e33-b81f6a14bd8e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147300 :question/problem "![](images/84/84f39f9d765a61db544fdddc7ee79859ab4a54c2e6f0e5018512723ca0dfcfd9.png)\n\n \n\nWhich of the nets above is **not** the net of a pyramid?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/72/72462d252e84e20d567ccd10c2be12a6496f442f08d6e6baa609c5fb74f6fcc5.png)\n\n     \n\nIf we were to fold the net above along its edges, then we'd get a triangular prism, as shown below: \n\n![](images/8e/8e77623f767c9cea456b787a09465397a4360915c547911a55927d8f7c9b4885.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the other two nets give us pyramids. Therefore,  the correct answer is I." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147621 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-776cd40d-1c79-55ee-9771-1ee0329ddc24"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147303 :question/problem "![](images/e4/e427a98c2953792d799190b7fc20a7dbf12ce014655316e21fb809e0abc9cdc5.png)\n\nWhich of the statements is true about the solids shown above?\n\nI. The net of solid I consists of triangles only.\n\nII. The net of solid II consists of $4$ triangles and $2$ rectangles.\n\nIII. The net of solid III consists of triangles only." :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the net of each solid.\n\n![](images/02/023f11b6924e6cf7318f54f5acdf910b1f688ee8ac40ec8f3b3ab7cd9c13c8df.png)\n\n \n\nNow, let's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false because the net of solid I consists of rectangles.\n\n- Statement II is false because the net of solid II consists of $2$ triangles and $3$ rectangles.\n\n- Statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-bcd25659-0e9d-5735-91bb-5b7182253798" :question/id #uuid "bcd25659-0e9d-5735-91bb-5b7182253798" :question/math-academy-id "q-62017" :question/problem "![](images/41/416f9df81e2159b58bddde964435f97fac3e461ce984402c2ea22616bc0edd48.png)\n\nThe net of which polyhedron is shown above?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/b2/b2ea30cd84f4d52f5d1e4a910817399c892c38a4b87ec7773eace67000a865fd.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIf we were to fold the net along its edges to form a solid shape, we'd get a rectangular pyramid.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/a0/a097a94ed0fa5ed23cf4e9b2ae36319ee2a00fb276b8b0bd1fe21999c1887f0f.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4f60d1e2-12c6-5cc1-a4cc-4b638feda7d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4f60d1e2-12c6-5cc1-a4cc-4b638feda7d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f60d1e2-12c6-5cc1-a4cc-4b638feda7d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ab150faf-4d93-57c4-9d2f-27b46dbd073a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-89326dea-bd92-5138-b928-1a6e4830905a" "answer-e65d907c-5a1d-57fd-8e94-b560140983ee" "answer-ab150faf-4d93-57c4-9d2f-27b46dbd073a" "answer-9fcf3df1-8581-5e33-8a79-888452dd1152" "answer-9a8d09df-249c-537c-95cc-c1ba4ffc2d34"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89326dea-bd92-5138-b928-1a6e4830905a" :answer/id #uuid "89326dea-bd92-5138-b928-1a6e4830905a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Cube" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e65d907c-5a1d-57fd-8e94-b560140983ee" :answer/id #uuid "e65d907c-5a1d-57fd-8e94-b560140983ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab150faf-4d93-57c4-9d2f-27b46dbd073a" :answer/id #uuid "ab150faf-4d93-57c4-9d2f-27b46dbd073a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Rectangular pyramid" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fcf3df1-8581-5e33-8a79-888452dd1152" :answer/id #uuid "9fcf3df1-8581-5e33-8a79-888452dd1152" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Triangular prism" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a8d09df-249c-537c-95cc-c1ba4ffc2d34" :answer/id #uuid "9a8d09df-249c-537c-95cc-c1ba4ffc2d34" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Triangular pyramid" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {: